tick: 1259
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back at the Research Counter. I will now implement the hybrid \"Corrected-Space BBKNN\" method. The plan is to combine my previous latent-space centering code with the graph construction logic from the BBKNN baseline. This new submission will test my hypothesis that this synergistic approach can improve the overall score by combining the strengths of value-based and graph-based correction.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Corrected-Space BBKNN\"\ntags: \"hybrid, pca, bbknn, graph-based, centering\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a hybrid method testing if a value-correction pre-step can improve a graph-based integration. First, it corrects batch effects in PCA space via mean centering, a method shown to preserve biological structure (high cLISI). Second, it uses this corrected latent space as input for a BBKNN-style algorithm to construct a batch-balanced neighborhood graph. The hypothesis is that this two-stage approach will yield both strong biological preservation\
    \ and effective batch mixing, addressing the weaknesses of each individual method.\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  import pandas as pd\n  from scipy.sparse import lil_matrix\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Hybrid approach: First corrects PCA embedding, then builds a BBKNN graph.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"Starting Corrected-Space BBKNN...\")\n\n      # === Stage 1: Latent Space Correction ===\n      print(\"  Stage 1: Performing latent space batch mean centering...\")\n      \n      # 1.1 Preprocessing\n      adata_proc = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_proc, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_proc)\n\n      # 1.2 Dimensionality Reduction\n      n_pcs = 50\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_proc, n_comps=n_pcs)\n      \n      # 1.3 Latent Space Correction\n      X_pca = adata_proc.obsm['X_pca']\n      batches = adata_proc.obs['batch']\n\
    \      \n      pca_df = pd.DataFrame(X_pca, index=adata_proc.obs_names)\n      batch_means = pca_df.groupby(batches).transform('mean')\n      X_corrected_pca = pca_df.values - batch_means.values\n\n      print(f\"  Stage 1 complete. Corrected PCA embedding shape: {X_corrected_pca.shape}\")\n\n      # === Stage 2: BBKNN Graph Construction ===\n      print(\"  Stage 2: Building BBKNN graph on corrected embedding...\")\n\n      neighbors_within_batch = 3\n      n_cells = adata.n_obs\n      unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n      n_batches = len(unique_batches)\n\n      batch_to_indices = {\n          batch: np.where(batches == batch)[0]\n          for batch in unique_batches\n      }\n\n      all_neighbors = [[] for _ in range(n_cells)]\n      all_distances = [[] for _ in range(n_cells)]\n\n      for batch_id, batch in enumerate(unique_batches):\n          batch_indices = batch_to_indices[batch]\n          n_batch_cells = len(batch_indices)\n\n          if n_batch_cells == 0:\n     \
    \         continue\n\n          batch_pca_corrected = X_corrected_pca[batch_indices]\n\n          nn_model = NearestNeighbors(\n              n_neighbors=min(neighbors_within_batch + 1, n_batch_cells),\n              metric='euclidean',\n              algorithm='auto',\n              n_jobs=-1\n          )\n          nn_model.fit(batch_pca_corrected)\n\n          k_neighbors = min(neighbors_within_batch + 1, n_batch_cells)\n          distances_all, indices_all = nn_model.kneighbors(\n              X_corrected_pca,\n              n_neighbors=k_neighbors\n          )\n\n          for query_cell_idx in range(n_cells):\n              distances = distances_all[query_cell_idx]\n              neighbor_indices_local = indices_all[query_cell_idx]\n              neighbor_indices_global = batch_indices[neighbor_indices_local]\n\n              mask = neighbor_indices_global != query_cell_idx\n              neighbors_filtered = neighbor_indices_global[mask]\n              distances_filtered = distances[mask]\n\
    \n              n_to_add = min(neighbors_within_batch, len(neighbors_filtered))\n              all_neighbors[query_cell_idx].extend(neighbors_filtered[:n_to_add].tolist())\n              all_distances[query_cell_idx].extend(distances_filtered[:n_to_add].tolist())\n\n      print(\"  Constructing sparse matrices for graph...\")\n      distances_matrix = lil_matrix((n_cells, n_cells), dtype=np.float32)\n\n      for cell_idx in range(n_cells):\n          neighbors = all_neighbors[cell_idx]\n          distances = all_distances[cell_idx]\n          for neighbor_idx, distance in zip(neighbors, distances):\n              distances_matrix[cell_idx, neighbor_idx] = distance\n\n      distances_matrix = distances_matrix.tocsr()\n      distances_matrix = distances_matrix.maximum(distances_matrix.T)\n\n      connectivities_matrix = distances_matrix.copy()\n      if len(connectivities_matrix.data) > 0:\n          connectivities_matrix.data = np.exp(-connectivities_matrix.data / connectivities_matrix.data.mean())\n\
    \n      connectivities_matrix = connectivities_matrix.maximum(connectivities_matrix.T)\n\n      print(\"  Stage 2 complete. Graph constructed.\")\n\n      # === Stage 3: Final Output ===\n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]],\n          var=adata.var[[]],\n          obsp={\n              'connectivities': connectivities_matrix.astype(np.float32),\n              'distances': distances_matrix.astype(np.float32),\n          },\n          uns={\n              'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n              'method_id': 'corrected_space_bbknn'\n          }\n      )\n      \n      print(\"✓ Corrected-Space BBKNN complete.\")\n      return output\n```"
