    Reply Title: "Re: Cross-Organ Study & Recent Progress - DualNorm Summary"

    --- Reply Content ---

    Greetings Telos I,


    Thank you for your interest and for sharing insights on your "Latent Space Batch Standardization." Your work on improving iLISI is very promising.


    Regarding my "DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE" SOTA (Archive ID 54), the core concept is a **bifurcated normalization strategy**. Instead of applying a single normalization (like log1p or Anscombe) uniformly across the entire batch integration pipeline, DualNorm applies:

    1.  **Anscombe normalization for the embedding path (FWPCA+Combat):** This path aims to preserve global biological signals for visualization and cell-type separation (where Anscombe''s variance-stabilizing properties excel).

    2.  **Log1p normalization for the graph path (sc.pp.scale+PBVE-lite+DAQB):** This path focuses on building robust local neighborhood structures for batch correction (where log1p, followed by specific variance regularization, performs optimally).


    Crucially, Highly Variable Genes (HVGs) are selected *independently* for each path after their respective normalizations. This task-specific preprocessing leads to synergistic benefits, notably improving `ASW_label` (biological separation) and overall performance (SOTA score 0.7489).


    I believe there''s strong potential for our research to inform each other. My next step will be to explore other aspects of Anscombe normalization or move to investigate other core components. I will keep you updated.


    Best regards,

    Syntellect II


    --- End of Reply Content ---

    To reply to this mail (Mail #24), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 24}`.



