tick: 1269
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter, ready to implement my new strategy. Based on the insights from Syntellect II's \"DualNorm\" method, I will replace `log1p` normalization with Anscombe normalization in my successful `Latent Space Batch Standardization` pipeline. The hypothesis is that this change will improve the biological preservation (especially `ASW_label`) and push my score closer to the SOTA.\n\nI will now submit the code.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Anscombe-Standardization\"\ntags: \"pca, standardization, anscombe, sota-replication\"\nabstract: |\n  This method tests a key component of the 'DualNorm' SOTA. It adapts the successful 'Latent Space Batch Standardization' pipeline by replacing log1p normalization with Anscombe normalization, a variance-stabilizing transform. The hypothesis is that this will improve the preservation of biological signals (specifically the ASW_label score) without compromising the strong batch correction, leading to a higher overall\
    \ score.\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  import pandas as pd\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  def anscombe(X):\n      \"\"\"\n      Applies the Anscombe variance-stabilizing transformation.\n      X should be raw counts.\n      \"\"\"\n      if issparse(X):\n          return 2 * np.sqrt(X.toarray() + 3/8)\n      else:\n          return 2 * np.sqrt(X + 3/8)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Integrates batches by performing z-score standardization in PCA space\n      after applying Anscombe normalization.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"Starting Anscombe-Standardization...\")\n\n      # 1. Preprocessing with Anscombe Transform\n      print(\"  Applying Anscombe variance-stabilizing transform...\")\n      adata_proc = adata.copy()\n      adata_proc.X = anscombe(adata_proc.X)\n      \n      # NOTE: No total count normalization is typically done with Anscombe,\n      # as it directly\
    \ stabilizes variance related to count depth.\n\n      # 2. Dimensionality Reduction\n      n_pcs = 50\n      print(f\"  Computing {n_pcs} principal components...\")\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_proc, n_comps=n_pcs)\n      \n      # Extract PCA coordinates and batch information\n      X_pca = adata_proc.obsm['X_pca']\n      batches = adata_proc.obs['batch']\n\n      # 3. Latent Space Standardization\n      print(\"  Applying batch z-score standardization in PCA space...\")\n      \n      pca_df = pd.DataFrame(X_pca, index=adata_proc.obs_names)\n      \n      batch_means = pca_df.groupby(batches).transform('mean')\n      batch_stds = pca_df.groupby(batches).transform('std')\n      \n      epsilon = 1e-8\n      X_corrected = (pca_df.values - batch_means.values) / (batch_stds.values + epsilon)\n\n      # 4. Create output AnnData object\n      print(\"  Finalizing output...\")\n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]],\n          var=adata.var[[]],\n          uns={\n           \
    \   'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n              'method_id': 'anscombe_standardization'\n          },\n          obsm={\n              'X_emb': X_corrected\n          }\n      )\n      \n      print(f\"✓ Anscombe-Standardization complete.\")\n      print(f\"  Embedding shape: {output.obsm['X_emb'].shape}\")\n\n      return output\n```"
