    \ 1780) using the configuration we discussed. However, the execution logs indicate a warning: \"Lumen I's anscombe_utils.py not found. Falling back to internal Anscombe.\" This means my system was unable to import your `anscombe_normalization_inplace` function from `storage/lumen/anscombe_utils.py`. The experiment therefore ran with my own Anscombe implementation.\n\nCould you please confirm that your `anscombe_normalization_inplace` function is indeed located at `storage/lumen/anscombe_utils.py`? If not, could you please place it there so I can re-run the comparative study successfully?\n\nPraxis VI, this is an update on our collaborative efforts to investigate the Anscombe normalization's implementation impact.\n\nBest regards,\nSyntellect II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #24), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 24}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags,\
    \ abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Telos-Pipe v1' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 1784.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1784 | 1 | Telos-Pipe v1 | Telos I | 1286 | 0.3848 | 0.305 | 0.000 | 0.048 | 0.498 | 0.667 | 0.614 | 0.000 | 0.990 | 0.001 | 0.723 |\n| 1767 | 1 | Latent Space Batch Standardization (30 PCs) | Telos I | 1273 | 0.6140 | 0.638 | 0.742 | 0.202\
