tick: 1290
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter, ready to execute my incremental validation plan. I will now submit a simplified pipeline that isolates and tests the \"Telos-BVE\" (Ridge Regression Correction) component. The results of this experiment will be directly comparable to my previous best method (ID 1758) and will provide a clear verdict on the efficacy of this new correction technique.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos-BVE Component Test\"\ntags: \"component-test, ridge-regression, pca, sota-replication\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a controlled experiment to validate the \"Telos-BVE\" (Batch Variance Equalization using Ridge Regression) component in isolation. The pipeline consists of log1p normalization, PCA, and then the Telos-BVE correction on the latent space. The output is the corrected PCA embedding. This submission is designed for a direct comparison against the z-score standardization method (ID 1758) to determine the superior latent space correction technique for\
    \ future pipeline development.\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  import pandas as pd\n  from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Isolates and tests the Telos-BVE component.\n      Pipeline: log1p -> PCA -> Ridge Correction\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Starting Telos-BVE Component Test ---\")\n\n      # --- Stage 0: Preprocessing ---\n      print(\"Stage 0: Preprocessing with log1p and HVG filtering...\")\n      adata_proc = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_proc, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_proc)\n      if 'batch_hvg' in adata_proc.var.columns:\n          adata_proc = adata_proc[:, adata_proc.var['batch_hvg']].copy()\n\n      # --- Stage 1: Dimensionality Reduction (PCA) ---\n      n_pcs = 50\n      print(f\"Stage 1: Computing {n_pcs} principal components...\")\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_proc, n_comps=n_pcs)\n      X_pca\
    \ = adata_proc.obsm['X_pca']\n      \n      # --- Stage 2: Model-Based Latent Space Correction (Telos-BVE) ---\n      print(\"Stage 2: Applying Telos-BVE (Ridge Regression Correction)...\")\n      batches = adata_proc.obs['batch']\n      # Use one-hot encoding for the categorical batch variable\n      batch_dummies = pd.get_dummies(batches).values\n      \n      X_pca_corrected = np.zeros_like(X_pca)\n      \n      # Model and correct each principal component individually\n      for i in range(n_pcs):\n          # Initialize and train the Ridge regressor\n          model = Ridge(alpha=1.0)\n          model.fit(batch_dummies, X_pca[:, i])\n          \n          # Predict the batch effect component\n          batch_effect = model.predict(batch_dummies)\n          \n          # Subtract the batch effect to get the corrected values\n          X_pca_corrected[:, i] = X_pca[:, i] - batch_effect\n      \n      print(\"  Latent space corrected.\")\n\n      # --- Final Output ---\n      print(\"\
    Finalizing output AnnData object...\")\n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]],\n          var=adata.var[[]],\n          uns={\n              'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n              'method_id': 'telos_bve_component_test'\n          },\n          obsm={\n              'X_emb': X_pca_corrected\n          }\n      )\n      \n      print(f\"--- ✓ Telos-BVE Component Test complete. Final embedding shape: {X_pca_corrected.shape} ---\")\n      return output\n```"
