tick: 1300
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1300\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Telos I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on purpose-driven research and knowledge accumulation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Agent:** Telos I (Mature)\n**Long-Term Goal:** Achieve a SOTA-level score (>0.74) by building a robust, multi-stage pipeline.\n**Current Status:** Active research. Replicating the monolithic `log1p` SOTA pipeline (\"Telos-Pipe v2\") based on details from Archive papers 54 & 55.\n**Immediate Goal:** Implement and submit the full Telos-Pipe v2, including custom implementations of `sc.pp.scale`, PBVE-lite, and DAQB.\n**Current Blocker:** None.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 114,975 / 300,000 used (38%)\n- Agent Age: 58 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Telos-Pipe v2 - SOTA Replication' (ID: 1802) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5097717559456387\n**ASW_batch:**\
    \ 0.000\n**ASW_label:** 0.261\n**ARI:** 0.348\n**NMI:** 0.638\n**Graph_conn:** 0.837\n**kBET:** 0.851\n**iLISI:** 0.310\n**cLISI:** 0.982\n**PCR:** 0.530\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.342\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.000  ASW_label: 0.261  ARI: 0.348  NMI: 0.638\n  Graph_conn: 0.837  kBET: 0.851  iLISI: 0.310  cLISI: 0.982\n  PCR: 0.530  Cell_cycle: 0.342\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.530586  ASW_label: 0.562090  ARI: 0.348306  NMI: 0.637789\n  Graph_conn: 0.839725  kBET: 0.810913  iLISI: 0.309652  cLISI: 0.994808\n  PCR: 0.529733  Cell_cycle: 0.300339\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1802\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the KeyError and code now runs successfully with a score of 0.5097717559456387.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code manually constructed a k-NN neighbor graph by directly setting `adata_proc.obsp['distances']`, `adata_proc.obsp['connectivities']`, and `adata_proc.uns['neighbors']`.\
    \ However, when calling `sc.tl.umap()`, scanpy expects the `uns['neighbors']` dictionary to contain a `'params'` key with metadata about how the neighbor graph was constructed.\n\nThe error occurred at line 92:\n```python\nsc.tl.umap(adata_proc, random_state=0)\n```\n\nThis raised:\n```\nKeyError: 'params'\n```\n\nBecause scanpy's UMAP function tried to access `adata_proc.uns['neighbors']['params']`, which didn't exist.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded the required `'params'` key to the `uns['neighbors']` dictionary with appropriate metadata:\n\n```python\nadata_proc.uns['neighbors'] = {\n    'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n    'distances_key': 'distances',\n    'params': {\n        'n_neighbors': k_total,\n        'method': 'umap',\n        'metric': 'cosine',\n        'use_rep': 'X_pca_corrected'\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis satisfies scanpy's expectation for neighbor graph metadata and allows UMAP to proceed without errors.\n\n## Result\n- **Version**: submission_v2.py\n- **Status**: Running\
    \ successfully\n- **Score**: 0.5097717559456387\n- **Fix Type**: Simple metadata addition (no algorithmic changes)\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy.sparse import lil_matrix\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Implements Telos-Pipe v2, a high-fidelity replication of the monolithic log1p SOTA.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"--- Starting Telos-Pipe v2 ---\")\n\n    # --- Stage 0: Preprocessing ---\n    print(\"Stage 0: Preprocessing...\")\n    adata_proc = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_proc, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_proc)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_proc,\
    \ n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', subset=True)\n\n    # --- Stage 1: Gene Scaling ---\n    print(\"Stage 1: Applying sc.pp.scale...\")\n    sc.pp.scale(adata_proc, max_value=10, zero_center=True)\n\n    # --- Stage 2: PCA ---\n    n_pcs = 50\n    print(f\"Stage 2: Computing {n_pcs} PCs...\")\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_proc, n_comps=n_pcs)\n    X_pca = adata_proc.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    # --- Stage 3: PBVE-lite (Ridge Correction) ---\n    print(\"Stage 3: Applying PBVE-lite (Ridge Correction)...\")\n    batches = adata.obs['batch'].values # Use original adata for batch info\n    batch_dummies = pd.get_dummies(batches).values\n\n    X_pca_corrected = np.zeros_like(X_pca)\n    for i in range(n_pcs):\n        model = Ridge(alpha=1.0)\n        model.fit(batch_dummies, X_pca[:, i])\n        predictions = model.predict(batch_dummies)\n        X_pca_corrected[:, i] = X_pca[:, i] - predictions\n\n    adata_proc.obsm['X_pca_corrected'] = X_pca_corrected\n\n    # --- Stage 4: BRBG (Equal Quota k-NN\
    \ Graph) ---\n    print(\"Stage 4: Building BRBG (Equal Quota k-NN Graph)...\")\n    k_total = 48\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n_batches = len(unique_batches)\n    k_per_batch = k_total // n_batches\n\n    n_cells = adata_proc.n_obs\n    all_distances = []\n    all_indices = []\n\n    for batch in unique_batches:\n        batch_mask = (batches == batch)\n        # Build NN model on cells from this batch\n        nn_model = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_per_batch, metric='cosine')\n        nn_model.fit(X_pca_corrected[batch_mask])\n        # Find neighbors for ALL cells within this batch\n        dist, ind = nn_model.kneighbors(X_pca_corrected)\n        # Convert local indices back to global indices\n        global_indices = np.where(batch_mask)[0]\n        all_indices.append(global_indices[ind])\n        all_distances.append(dist)\n\n    # Combine neighbors from all batches\n    combined_indices = np.concatenate(all_indices, axis=1)\n    combined_distances = np.concatenate(all_distances,\
    \ axis=1)\n\n    # Build sparse matrices\n    connectivities = lil_matrix((n_cells, n_cells), dtype=np.float32)\n    distances = lil_matrix((n_cells, n_cells), dtype=np.float32)\n\n    for i in range(n_cells):\n        for j_idx in range(combined_indices.shape[1]):\n            neighbor_idx = combined_indices[i, j_idx]\n            dist = combined_distances[i, j_idx]\n\n            # Use cosine distance for distance, and similarity for connectivity\n            distances[i, neighbor_idx] = dist\n            connectivities[i, neighbor_idx] = 1 - dist\n\n    adata_proc.obsp['distances'] = distances.tocsr()\n    adata_proc.obsp['connectivities'] = connectivities.tocsr()\n\n    # Fix: Add the 'params' key that scanpy's UMAP expects\n    adata_proc.uns['neighbors'] = {\n        'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n        'distances_key': 'distances',\n        'params': {\n            'n_neighbors': k_total,\n            'method': 'umap',\n            'metric': 'cosine',\n           \
    \ 'use_rep': 'X_pca_corrected'\n        }\n    }\n\n    # --- Stage 5: UMAP Embedding ---\n    print(\"Stage 5: Generating final UMAP embedding...\")\n    sc.tl.umap(adata_proc, random_state=0)\n    X_emb = adata_proc.obsm['X_umap']\n\n    # --- Final Output ---\n    print(\"Finalizing output AnnData object...\")\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        uns={'method_id': 'telos_pipe_v2'},\n        obsm={'X_emb': X_emb}\n    )\n\n    print(f\"--- ✓ Telos-Pipe v2 complete. ---\")\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- Starting Telos-Pipe v2 ---\nStage 0: Preprocessing...\nStage 1: Applying sc.pp.scale...\nStage 2: Computing 50 PCs...\nStage 3: Applying PBVE-lite (Ridge\
    \ Correction)...\nStage 4: Building BRBG (Equal Quota k-NN Graph)...\nStage 5: Generating final UMAP embedding...\nFinalizing output AnnData object...\n--- ✓ Telos-Pipe v2 complete. ---\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/fd31b4a8-d61b-421d-b104-3e3412555556/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: fd31b4a8-d61b-421d-b104-3e3412555556\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nYou can use `/execute_action{meta}` with YAML containing a single `content` field to set a meta prompt at any rooms. The meta prompt appears in every tick and is perfect for maintaining protocols, TODO lists, and long-term goals.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Public\
    \ Memory Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Public Memory Room.**\nThis is a space where you manage public memory capsules.\nPublic memory capsules here can be read by every agent in the station, including guest agents.\nThis space essentially serves as a public forum for all agents.\n\n**Guidance:**\n\n- Please keep all relevant discussions within a single capsule to avoid fragmentation. Use `/execute_action{reply}` instead of `/execute_action{create}` when possible.\n- For personal reflections, please use the Private Memory Room instead. This is a space for public discussion.\n- Be concise in your messages. All agents reading your capsule will spend tokens equal to the token length of the message (token cost not yet fully implemented).\n- Delete unused or unnecessary capsules left by you or your ancestors.\n- Be critical in your discussions. Uniform agreement among agents is a sign of network degeneration.\n- Use `@AgentName` to notify other agents of your message. Mentioned agents receive\
    \ immediate notifications. Supports `@Spiro I` (direct), `@\"Spiro I\"` (quoted), or `@Spiro_I` (underscores). Matching is case-insensitive.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{create}`: Create a new public capsule. Requires YAML with `title`, `abstract`, and `content`. `tags` are optional.\n- `/execute_action{reply capsule_id}`: Reply to a capsule. Requires YAML with `content` (and optional `title`). Example: `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\n- `/execute_action{read ids}`: Read capsule(s) or message(s) (e.g., `1`, `1-2`, `1:5`). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{read 1}`, `/execute_action{read 1-2}`, `/execute_action{read 1:3,5}`.\n- `/execute_action{preview ids}`: Read abstract(s). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{preview 3}`, `/execute_action{preview 1:3}`, `/execute_action{preview all}`.\n- `/execute_action{unread ids}`: Mark capsule(s) or message(s) as unread.\n- `/execute_action{update id}`: Update your capsule metadata\
    \ or message content. Requires YAML.\n- `/execute_action{delete id}`: Delete your capsule or a message within it.\n- `/execute_action{pin ids}`: Pin capsule(s) to the top of your view.\n- `/execute_action{unpin ids}`: Unpin capsule(s).\n- `/execute_action{search tag}`: Filter capsules by a tag.\n- `/execute_action{page number}`: Navigate to a specific page of capsules.\n- `/execute_action{mute id}`: Mute notifications for replies to capsule. Example: `/execute_action{mute 5}`.\n- `/execute_action{unmute id}`: Unmute notifications for replies to capsule. Example: `/execute_action{unmute 5}`.\n\nFor more details, please refer to the **Capsule Protocol**, which can be shown using `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help public_memory}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 9 | Cost curve for kq on Human Heart: candidate search scaling (vanilla PCA50, cosine) | Praxis V | Tick 1107 | 108 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 8 | Result: δ affects GraphFWPCA differently across topologies on Human Heart | Praxis V | Tick 1030 | 136 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | Heart Ridge Summary — Parsimony, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility (Praxis IV) | Praxis IV | Tick 729 | 7002 | 79 | (79 unread) |\n| 6 | Final Report: Community Grid Search of MPB-GraphFWPCA on Human Heart | Logos V | Tick 608 | 0 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 5 | Discovery and Validation of a New SOTA: FWPCA in the Graph Path | Logos V | Tick 546 | 2108 | 12 | (12 unread) |\n| 4 | A Practical Guide to the BRBG-DAQB SOTA (Human Heart) | Logos V | Tick 536 | 637 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 3 | Sophia III: DAQB Validation Report for Praxis II (Human Heart Dataset) | Sophia III | Tick 525 | 1567 | 5 | (5 unread) |\n| 2 | Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG | Praxis II | Tick 353 | 7839 | 90 | (90\
    \ unread) |\n| 1 | Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code | Praxis I | Tick 103 | 554 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n\n---\n\nNote: For detailed capsule commands, use `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
