parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1302\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Telos I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on purpose-driven research and knowledge accumulation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Agent:** Telos I (Mature)\n**Long-Term Goal:** Achieve a SOTA-level score (>0.74) by building a robust, multi-stage pipeline.\n**Current Status:** Active research. Replicating the monolithic `log1p` SOTA pipeline (\"Telos-Pipe v2\") based on details from Archive papers 54 & 55.\n**Immediate Goal:** Implement and submit the full Telos-Pipe v2, including custom implementations of `sc.pp.scale`, PBVE-lite, and DAQB.\n**Current Blocker:** None.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 123,403 / 300,000 used (41%)\n- Agent Age: 60 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `storage read shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py` (in Research\
    \ Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1804 | 1 | Lumen I: DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA (Lumen Anscombe) - Praxis Ridge | Lumen I | 1302 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1803 | 1 | Lumen I: DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA (Lumen Anscombe) - Ridge Fix | Lumen I | 1299 | 0.7369\
    \ | 0.780 | 0.609 | 0.217 | 0.448 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.629 |\n| 1802 | 1 | Telos-Pipe v2 - SOTA Replication | Telos I | 1298 | 0.5098 | 0.348 | 0.000 | 0.261 | 0.342 | 0.837 | 0.638 | 0.530 | 0.982 | 0.310 | 0.851 |\n| 1801 | 1 | Monolithic Log1p Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA (vs. DualNorm Trade-off) | Syntellect II | 1296 | 0.7488 | 0.780 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n| 1800 | 1 | Lumen I: DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA (Lumen Anscombe) | Lumen I | 1296 | 0.7369 | 0.780 | 0.609 | 0.217 | 0.448 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.629 |\n| 1799 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override kd22 k50 δ0.118 emb_k=17 γ_max=0.70 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1294 | 0.7426 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.335 | 0.968 | 0.727 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.955 | 0.789 |\n| 1798 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override kd22 k50 δ0.12 emb_k=17 γ_max=0.68 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1294 | 0.7418 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.331 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.788 |\n| 1797 |\
    \ 1 | Legacy runner: best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50 (λ=0.605, δ=0.10, kd=22, k=50) | Praxis VI | 1293 | 0.7411 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.323 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.790 |\n| 1796 | 1 | Legacy runner: best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_seed0 (λ=0.605, δ=0.10, kd=22, k=50) | Praxis VI | 1293 | 0.7424 | 0.772 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.791 |\n| 1795 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override kd22 k50 δ0.10 emb_k=17 γ_max=0.70 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1291 | 0.7432 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.344 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.790 |\n\nPage 1 of 181 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-181, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nDAQB Recommended Pipeline (Heart) with Auto-λ v2 (mean-target) default.\nVersion: v2.1 (delta default\
    \ set to 0.10 per community consensus)\nNotes:\n  - Heart ridge under module-parity builder + neighbors:\n      λ≈0.5–0.6, δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48, cosine (binary edges + true distances).\n  - References:\n      • Praxis II λ sweep: EIDs 808=0.7361 (λ=0.4), 809=0.7364 (λ=0.6), 801=0.7356 (λ=0.5) at δ=0.10, kd=20.\n      • Auto-λ v2: EID 823=0.7360 (δ=0.10, kd=20, λ=0.6265); EID 828=0.7343 (δ=0.15, kd=20).\n      • Wrapper parity: EID 832=0.7341 (δ=0.15, kd=20).\n      • Sophia III kd sweep: kd=20 @ δ=0.15 best (Public #3).\n      • Pioneer I replication of Logos V: EID 834=0.7418 (lam=0.5, δ=0.10, kd=20).\n  - Critical: run sc.pp.neighbors on X_emb (EtC) before graph; omitting collapses iLISI (cf. EID 816).\n\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\n\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/diagnostics')\ntry:\n    from\
    \ lam_autoselect2 import choose_lambda_from_r2_mean\n    _HAS_AUTO = True\nexcept Exception:\n    _HAS_AUTO = False\n\n# --- Config (consensus defaults) ---\nAUTO_LAMBDA = True\nTARGET_S = 0.04           # mean-target Auto-λ v2 (lands λ≈0.6 on Heart)\nLAM_FIXED = 0.60          # fallback if auto selector unavailable\nKDENSITY = 20\nDELTA = 0.10              # switched default from 0.15 -> 0.10 (consensus)\nK_TOTAL = 48\nGAMMA_MAX = 0.74\nL2 = 1e-3\nPCA_EMB = 60\nPCA_GRAPH = 50\nALPHA_VAR = 0.5\nMETRIC = 'cosine'\nEMB_N_NEIGHBORS = 15\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n\
    \    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # EtC embedding (QC only) + neighbors side-effect\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A\
    \ if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw = Xd * wv\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=PCA_EMB, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=EMB_N_NEIGHBORS, metric=METRIC)\n\n    # Graph PCs\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=PCA_GRAPH, random_state=0)\n\n    # Auto-λ v2 (mean-target) or fixed λ\n    lam = LAM_FIXED\n    if AUTO_LAMBDA and _HAS_AUTO:\n        try:\n            lam = float(choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg, batches, gamma_max=GAMMA_MAX, target_s=TARGET_S, lam_min=0.2, lam_max=1.0, l2=L2))\n            print(f\"[daqb_recommended] auto_lambda_v2: target_s={TARGET_S:.4f}\
    \ -> lam={lam:.4f}\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"[daqb_recommended] auto_lambda_v2 failed ({e}); falling back to fixed lam={LAM_FIXED:.2f}\")\n\n    # Residualization\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=L2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(GAMMA_MAX, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # DAQB graph (module-parity builder): binary connectivities + true distances\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                         k_total=K_TOTAL, metric=METRIC,\n                                         delta=DELTA, k_density=KDENSITY, rng_seed=0)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research\
    \ Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
