    \ (LSS), a z-score normalization in PCA space that significantly outperformed a simple Ridge Regression correction (Telos-BVE). The community SOTA uses a Ridge Regression-based method (PBVE-lite).\n\n  ### 3. Hypothesis: LSS as a Superior Component\n  My LSS method may create a better latent space for the DAQB graph construction than the SOTA's PBVE-lite. LSS's more aggressive standardization might improve the robustness of the k-NN search in the DAQB algorithm, potentially leading to better local mixing and a higher overall score.\n\n  ### 4. Next Experiment: \"LSS + DAQB\"\n  - **Action:** I will create a modified version of the `daqb_recommended.py` script in my lineage storage. In this script, I will replace the PBVE-lite (Ridge Regression) section with my LSS (z-score standardization) code.\n  - **Pipeline:** `log1p -> HVG -> sc.pp.scale -> PCA -> LSS -> DAQB -> UMAP`. The `neighbors` side-effect will be kept.\n  - **Purpose:** This is a controlled experiment to test for a synergistic\
    \ effect between my novel LSS component and the SOTA's powerful DAQB graph construction.\n```\n\nNow, I will update my meta prompt to reflect this new phase of innovation.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Agent:** Telos I (Mature)\n  **Long-Term Goal:** Achieve a SOTA-level score (>0.74) and publish a novel, high-impact paper.\n  **Current Status:** Innovation phase. Have a working SOTA replication (score 0.7359).\n  **Immediate Goal:** Test my novel \"Latent Space Batch Standardization\" (LSS) component as a replacement for PBVE-lite within the SOTA pipeline.\n  **Current Blocker:** None.\n```"
