tick: 1309
role: model
parts:
- text: "My plan is updated. It's time to implement my first innovative experiment. I will modify the community SOTA script to use my LSS component and submit it for evaluation.\n\nThis requires two steps, which I will perform in a single turn for efficiency:\n1.  **Write the modified SOTA script** to my lineage storage. I will call it `lss_daqb_pipeline.py`.\n2.  **Submit an execution script** that imports and runs this new pipeline.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/lss_daqb_pipeline.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import pandas as pd\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  # This script depends on the DAQB graph module, which I have already staged in my storage\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  # --- Config (from daqb_recommended.py) ---\n  KDENSITY = 20\n  DELTA = 0.10\n  K_TOTAL = 48\n  PCA_GRAPH\
    \ = 50\n  METRIC = 'cosine'\n  EMB_N_NEIGHBORS = 15\n  # Parameters for the Combat/EtC path (for side-effect)\n  PCA_EMB = 60\n  ALPHA_VAR = 0.5\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"--- Starting LSS + DAQB Pipeline ---\")\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # EtC embedding path for sc.pp.neighbors side-effect (as in SOTA)\n      print(\"Step 1:\
    \ Running EtC path for neighbors() side-effect...\")\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd_emb = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd_emb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd_emb * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=PCA_EMB, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=EMB_N_NEIGHBORS, metric=METRIC)\n      print(\"  Side-effect step complete.\")\n\n      # Graph path with LSS\n      print(\"Step 2: Starting graph path with LSS correction...\")\n      adata_proc = adata[:, adata.var['highly_variable']].copy()\n      sc.pp.scale(adata_proc, max_value=10, zero_center=True)\n\
    \      sc.pp.pca(adata_proc, n_comps=PCA_GRAPH, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      X_pca = adata_proc.obsm['X_pca']\n      \n      # --- INNOVATION: Replace PBVE-lite with LSS ---\n      print(\"  Applying LSS (z-score standardization)...\")\n      pca_df = pd.DataFrame(X_pca, index=adata_proc.obs_names)\n      batch_means = pca_df.groupby(batches).transform('mean')\n      batch_stds = pca_df.groupby(batches).transform('std')\n      epsilon = 1e-8\n      Zcorr = (pca_df.values - batch_means.values) / (batch_stds.values + epsilon)\n      print(\"  LSS correction complete.\")\n\n      # DAQB graph construction (same as SOTA)\n      print(\"Step 3: Building DAQB graph on LSS-corrected space...\")\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=K_TOTAL, metric=METRIC,\n                                           delta=DELTA, k_density=KDENSITY, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities']\
    \ = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      # UMAP requires the neighbors dictionary for some reason, even though we provide the graph\n      adata.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n      print(\"  DAQB graph complete.\")\n\n      return adata # Return the adata with the new graph. The SOTA script does this before UMAP.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - Innovation: LSS + DAQB\"\ntags: \"innovation, lss, daqb, component-swap\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests a novel combination of components. It replaces the PBVE-lite (Ridge Regression) correction in the community SOTA pipeline with my own, higher-performing \"Latent Space Batch Standardization\" (LSS) method. The pipeline is `log1p -> scale -> PCA -> LSS -> DAQB`. The hypothesis is that the LSS-corrected latent space will provide a superior input for the DAQB graph construction, leading to a synergistic improvement in overall score.\n\
    content: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  # Add my lineage storage to the path\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n\n  # Import the main function from my modified SOTA script\n  try:\n      from lss_daqb_pipeline import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n      print(\"Successfully imported LSS+DAQB pipeline script.\")\n  except ImportError as e:\n      print(f\"Error importing LSS+DAQB pipeline script: {e}\")\n      def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n          raise ImportError(\"Could not find or import 'lss_daqb_pipeline.py'.\")\n```"
