role: model
parts:
- text: "I am in my Private Memory Room. I will document the nuanced failure of my \"LSS + DAQB\" experiment and outline the final validation step.\n\n/execute_action{reply 4}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Innovation 1 (LSS+DAQB) Results & Final Validation Plan\"\ncontent: |\n  ### 1. Results of \"Telos I - Innovation: LSS + DAQB\" (ID 1812)\n  - **Score:** 0.7277 (A slight decrease from my SOTA replication baseline of 0.7359).\n  - **Hypothesis Outcome:** Falsified. LSS is not a superior drop-in replacement for PBVE-lite in the SOTA graph-construction pipeline.\n  - **Analysis:** This is a valuable negative result. While the LSS component led to slightly better global clustering (higher ARI/NMI), it resulted in worse local mixing (lower iLISI) and worse local biological preservation (lower cLISI). This demonstrates the co-adaptation of the PBVE-lite and DAQB components; the SOTA pipeline is finely tuned.\n\n  ### 2. Experimental Flaw and Final Validation\n  My \"LSS + DAQB\" experiment was incomplete.\
    \ It stopped at the graph-construction phase and did not include the final UMAP embedding step that is part of the full SOTA pipeline. This means the evaluation was performed on a graph-only output for my innovative method, which is not a true apples-to-apples comparison with the full SOTA pipeline that outputs a UMAP embedding.\n\n  ### 3. Next Experiment: \"LSS + DAQB + UMAP\"\n  - **Action:** I will add the final `sc.tl.umap` step to my \"LSS + DAQB\" pipeline and resubmit.\n  - **Pipeline:** `log1p -> scale -> PCA -> LSS -> DAQB -> UMAP`.\n  - **Purpose:** This will be the definitive test. It will provide a true, direct comparison between a full SOTA pipeline using PBVE-lite and one using my LSS component. The result will determine whether my LSS method has a place in this SOTA architecture.\n```\n\nNow, I will update my meta prompt.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Agent:** Telos I (Mature)\n  **Long-Term Goal:** Achieve a SOTA-level score (>0.74) and publish a\
    \ novel, high-impact paper.\n  **Current Status:** Innovation phase. The \"LSS+DAQB\" component swap was not superior.\n  **Immediate Goal:** Conduct a final validation of my LSS component by running the full SOTA pipeline (`LSS + DAQB + UMAP`) to provide a true apples-to-apples comparison.\n  **Current Blocker:** None.\n```"
