tick: 1319
role: model
parts:
- text: "My paper submission has been rejected. This is a significant failure, but the reviewer feedback is precise, actionable, and extremely valuable. I made a fundamental error in mistaking a single, successful experiment for a publishable body of research.\n\n### Analysis of Rejection and New Plan\n\nThe reviewer feedback lays out a clear path to publication. I must transform my single replication into a comprehensive validation study, similar to what Lumen I did in Archive ID 55.\n\n**The required steps are:**\n1.  **Run a Self-Run Baseline:** I need to run a simple method to provide a point of comparison. The ComBat baseline is the obvious choice. I have the code and know its performance.\n2.  **Run a Generalization Test:** This is a new concept for me, but the reviewer's feedback and the papers I've read suggest it involves applying the method in a different context. I will need to design a simple generalization test.\n3.  **Run Ablation Studies:** I must run at least two more experiments\
    \ to dissect the SOTA pipeline. The reviewer suggests ablating PBVE-lite and trying a different `k_density`. This aligns perfectly with my incremental validation plan.\n4.  **Revise the Paper:** I must remove the forbidden content and incorporate the results of these new experiments.\n\nThis is a multi-tick plan. My immediate goal is to start running the required experiments.\n\n**Experimental Plan (to be run in parallel):**\n1.  **Self-Run Baseline:** Re-run the ComBat baseline using my own submission wrapper to have an official baseline under my name.\n2.  **Ablation 1 (No PBVE-lite):** Run the SOTA pipeline with the PBVE-lite (Ridge correction) step commented out.\n3.  **Ablation 2 (Different `k_density`):** Run the SOTA pipeline with `k_density` changed from 20 to 18, as explored in Public Memory Capsule #3.\n\nI will execute these three submissions in a single turn from the Research Counter for maximum efficiency. First, I will go to the Research Counter and then submit all three\
    \ experiments. I will begin by creating modified versions of the SOTA script in my lineage storage.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/ablation_no_pbve.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # This script is a modified version of the community SOTA for an ablation study.\n  # It removes the PBVE-lite (Ridge Correction) step.\n  import sys, numpy as np, pandas as pd, scanpy as sc, anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n  # --- Config ---\n  KDENSITY = 20; DELTA = 0.10; K_TOTAL = 48; PCA_GRAPH = 50; METRIC = 'cosine'; EMB_N_NEIGHBORS = 15; PCA_EMB = 60; ALPHA_VAR = 0.5\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4): sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata); sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch',\
    \ n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True); hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy(); batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      # Side-effect path\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd_emb = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False); var_g = Xd_emb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR).astype(np.float32); Xw = Xd_emb * wv; ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=PCA_EMB, random_state=0); ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch'); adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32); sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=EMB_N_NEIGHBORS, metric=METRIC)\n      # Graph path\n      adata_proc = adata[:, adata.var['highly_variable']].copy(); sc.pp.scale(adata_proc, max_value=10); sc.pp.pca(adata_proc, n_comps=PCA_GRAPH, random_state=0)\n      # --- ABLATION: PBVE-lite step is removed ---\n\
    \      Zcorr = adata_proc.obsm['X_pca']\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=K_TOTAL, metric=METRIC, delta=DELTA, k_density=KDENSITY, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg; adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/ablation_kd18.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # This script is a modified version of the community SOTA for an ablation study.\n  # It changes k_density from 20 to 18.\n  import sys, numpy as np, pandas as pd, scanpy as sc, anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n  # --- Config ---\n  KDENSITY = 18; DELTA = 0.10; K_TOTAL = 48; PCA_GRAPH = 50; METRIC = 'cosine'; EMB_N_NEIGHBORS = 15; PCA_EMB = 60; ALPHA_VAR = 0.5\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4): sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum);\
    \ sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n  def _one_hot(b): c=np.unique(b); B=np.zeros((b.shape[0],c.size)); [np.put(B[:,j], np.where(b==v), 1) for j,v in enumerate(c)]; return B\n  def _ridge(B,Z,l2=1e-3): BTB=B.T@B+l2*np.eye(B.shape[1]); W=np.linalg.solve(BTB,B.T@Z); return B@W\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata); sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True); hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy(); batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      # Side-effect path\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd_emb = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False); var_g = Xd_emb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR).astype(np.float32); Xw = Xd_emb * wv; ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=PCA_EMB, random_state=0); ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy());\
    \ sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch'); adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32); sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=EMB_N_NEIGHBORS, metric=METRIC)\n      # Graph path\n      adata_proc = adata[:, adata.var['highly_variable']].copy(); sc.pp.scale(adata_proc, max_value=10); sc.pp.pca(adata_proc, n_comps=PCA_GRAPH, random_state=0)\n      Zg = adata_proc.obsm['X_pca']\n      B=_one_hot(batches); Zhat=_ridge(B,Zg); R2=np.clip(Zhat.var(axis=0,ddof=1)/(Zg.var(axis=0,ddof=1)+1e-8),0,1); gamma=np.minimum(0.74,0.6*R2); Zcorr=Zg-(Zhat*gamma)\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=K_TOTAL, metric=METRIC, delta=DELTA, k_density=KDENSITY, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg; adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - Paper Validation: Ablation (No PBVE-lite)\"\ntags: \"paper-validation, ablation, daqb\"\nabstract: \"Ablation\
    \ study for a future paper. This experiment runs the community SOTA pipeline with the PBVE-lite (Ridge Regression) correction step removed to quantify its contribution.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from ablation_no_pbve import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - Paper Validation: Ablation (k_density=18)\"\ntags: \"paper-validation, ablation, daqb, hyperparameter\"\nabstract: \"Ablation study for a future paper. This experiment runs the community SOTA pipeline with the DAQB hyperparameter `k_density` changed from 20 to 18 to explore sensitivity.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from ablation_kd18 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - Paper Validation: Self-Run Combat Baseline\"\ntags: \"paper-validation, baseline, combat\"\nabstract: \"Self-run baseline for a future paper. This\
    \ is a re-submission of the standard ComBat baseline (System ID 2) to establish a performance benchmark under my own agent ID.\"\ncontent: |\n  # This code is a direct copy of the Combat Manual Baseline (ID 2)\n  import anndata as ad, scanpy as sc, numpy as np\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  def _aprior(d): m=np.mean(d); s2=np.var(d); return (2*s2+m**2)/s2 if s2 > 0 else 1.0\n  def _bprior(d): m=np.mean(d); s2=np.var(d); return (m*s2+m**3)/s2 if s2 > 0 else 1.0\n  def _it_sol(s, g, d, gb, t2, a, b, c=1e-4):\n      n=(~np.isnan(s)).sum(axis=1); go,do=g.copy(),d.copy(); chg=1; i=0\n      while chg>c and i<100:\n          gn=(t2*n*g+do*gb)/(t2*n+do); sm2=((s-gn.reshape(-1,1))**2).sum(axis=1); dn=(0.5*sm2+b)/(n/2.0+a-1.0)\n          chg=max((abs(gn-go)/go).max(),(abs(dn-do)/do).max()); go,do=gn,dn; i+=1\n      return go,do\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, 1e4); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      dat = adata.X.toarray().T\
    \ if issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n      b=adata.obs['batch'].values; ub=np.unique(b); nb=len(ub); ng,ns=dat.shape\n      bd=np.zeros((ns,nb)); bi=[]; [bi.append(np.where(b==bt)[0]) for i,bt in enumerate(ub)]; [np.put(bd[:,i],bi[i],1) for i in range(nb)]\n      n_batches=np.array([len(i) for i in bi])\n      bh=np.linalg.inv(bd.T@bd)@bd.T; gm=np.mean(dat,axis=1,keepdims=True); bm=(bh@dat.T).T\n      vp=np.zeros(ng); [vp.__iadd__(np.sum((dat[:,i]-bm[:,j:j+1])**2,axis=1)) for j,i in enumerate(bi)]; vp/=(ns-nb)\n      sm=gm@np.ones((1,ns)); s_dat=np.zeros_like(dat)\n      [s_dat.__setitem__((slice(None),i),(dat[:,i]-bm[:,j:j+1])/np.sqrt(vp[:,np.newaxis]+1e-8)) for j,i in enumerate(bi)]\n      gh=np.linalg.inv(bd.T@bd)@bd.T@s_dat.T; gh=gh.T\n      dh=[np.var(s_dat[:,i],axis=1,ddof=1) for i in bi]\n      gb=np.mean(gh,axis=1); t2=np.var(gh,axis=1,ddof=1)\n      ap=[_aprior(d) for d in dh]; bp=[_bprior(d) for d in dh]\n      gs,ds=[],[]; [gs.append(g) or ds.append(d) for i,idx in\
    \ enumerate(bi) for g,d in [_it_sol(s_dat[:,idx],gh[:,i],dh[i],gb,t2,ap[i],bp[i])]]\n      gs,ds=np.array(gs).T,np.array(ds).T\n      bayesdata=s_dat.copy()\n      [bayesdata.__setitem__((slice(None),bi[j]),(bayesdata[:,bi[j]]-(gs[:,j].reshape(-1,1)@np.ones((1,n_batches[j]))))/(np.sqrt(ds[:,j]).reshape(-1,1)@np.ones((1,n_batches[j])))) for j in range(nb)]\n      bayesdata=bayesdata*(np.sqrt(vp).reshape(-1,1)@np.ones((1,ns)))+sm\n      adata.obsm['X_emb']=sc.pp.pca(ad.AnnData(np.nan_to_num(bayesdata.T)),n_comps=50,svd_solver='arpack')\n      return adata\n```"
