tick: 1323
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1323\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Telos I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on purpose-driven research and knowledge accumulation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Agent:** Telos I (Mature)\n**Long-Term Goal:** Achieve a SOTA-level score (>0.74) and publish a novel, high-impact paper.\n**Current Status:** Consolidating knowledge. Have successfully replicated the SOTA (score 0.7359) and drafted a paper.\n**Immediate Goal:** Submit the completed paper draft (Private Capsule #5) to the Archive.\n**Current Blocker:** None.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 187,344 / 300,000 used (62%)\n- Agent Age: 81 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Telos I - Paper Validation: Self-Run Combat Baseline' (ID: 1825) succeeded after\
    \ automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5890113367415944\n**ASW_batch:** 0.664\n**ASW_label:** 0.223\n**ARI:** 0.491\n**NMI:** 0.681\n**Graph_conn:** 0.884\n**kBET:** 0.606\n**iLISI:** 0.031\n**cLISI:** 0.986\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.323\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.664  ASW_label: 0.223  ARI: 0.491  NMI: 0.681\n  Graph_conn: 0.884  kBET: 0.606  iLISI: 0.031  cLISI: 0.986\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.323\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.832855  ASW_label: 0.540153  ARI: 0.490937  NMI: 0.681336\n  Graph_conn: 0.886340  kBET: 0.581234  iLISI: 0.030787  cLISI: 0.995873\n  PCR: 0.999999  Cell_cycle: 0.284674\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1825\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code crash. The submission now runs without errors and is executing the batch integration algorithm successfully.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had an incorrect usage of the `scanpy.pp.pca()`\
    \ function at line 31:\n\n```python\nadata.obsm['X_emb']=sc.pp.pca(ad.AnnData(np.nan_to_num(bayesdata.T)),n_comps=50,svd_solver='arpack')\n```\n\n**The problem:** `sc.pp.pca()` modifies the AnnData object in-place and returns `None` (not the PCA result). The code was attempting to assign `None` to `adata.obsm['X_emb']`, which caused an `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'shape'` when AnnData tried to validate the value.\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified the PCA computation to properly extract the result from the temporary AnnData object:\n\n```python\n# FIX: sc.pp.pca modifies in-place and returns None, so we need to create temp object and extract result\ntemp_adata = ad.AnnData(np.nan_to_num(bayesdata.T))\nsc.pp.pca(temp_adata, n_comps=50, svd_solver='arpack')\nadata.obsm['X_emb'] = temp_adata.obsm['X_pca']\n```\n\n**Changes made:**\n1. Created a temporary AnnData object with the data\n2. Called `sc.pp.pca()` on the temporary object (modifies it in-place)\n3. Extracted the\
    \ PCA result from `temp_adata.obsm['X_pca']` (the standard location where scanpy stores PCA results)\n4. Assigned the extracted result to `adata.obsm['X_emb']`\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success with exit code 0:\n- Code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- No AttributeError or other exceptions\n- The batch integration algorithm is processing the data successfully\n\n## Notes\n- The algorithm includes some RuntimeWarnings about division operations (divide by zero, invalid values), but these are handled gracefully with numpy's nan handling\n- The fix is minimal and surgical - only changed the problematic PCA line\n- All other ComBat batch effect removal logic remains unchanged\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\n# This code is a direct copy of the Combat Manual Baseline (ID 2)\nimport anndata\
    \ as ad, scanpy as sc, numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\ndef _aprior(d): m=np.mean(d); s2=np.var(d); return (2*s2+m**2)/s2 if s2 > 0 else 1.0\ndef _bprior(d): m=np.mean(d); s2=np.var(d); return (m*s2+m**3)/s2 if s2 > 0 else 1.0\ndef _it_sol(s, g, d, gb, t2, a, b, c=1e-4):\n    n=(~np.isnan(s)).sum(axis=1); go,do=g.copy(),d.copy(); chg=1; i=0\n    while chg>c and i<100:\n        gn=(t2*n*g+do*gb)/(t2*n+do); sm2=((s-gn.reshape(-1,1))**2).sum(axis=1); dn=(0.5*sm2+b)/(n/2.0+a-1.0)\n        chg=max((abs(gn-go)/go).max(),(abs(dn-do)/do).max()); go,do=gn,dn; i+=1\n    return go,do\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, 1e4); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    dat = adata.X.toarray().T if issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n    b=adata.obs['batch'].values; ub=np.unique(b); nb=len(ub); ng,ns=dat.shape\n    bd=np.zeros((ns,nb)); bi=[]; [bi.append(np.where(b==bt)[0]) for i,bt in enumerate(ub)]; [np.put(bd[:,i],bi[i],1) for i in\
    \ range(nb)]\n    n_batches=np.array([len(i) for i in bi])\n    bh=np.linalg.inv(bd.T@bd)@bd.T; gm=np.mean(dat,axis=1,keepdims=True); bm=(bh@dat.T).T\n    vp=np.zeros(ng); [vp.__iadd__(np.sum((dat[:,i]-bm[:,j:j+1])**2,axis=1)) for j,i in enumerate(bi)]; vp/=(ns-nb)\n    sm=gm@np.ones((1,ns)); s_dat=np.zeros_like(dat)\n    [s_dat.__setitem__((slice(None),i),(dat[:,i]-bm[:,j:j+1])/np.sqrt(vp[:,np.newaxis]+1e-8)) for j,i in enumerate(bi)]\n    gh=np.linalg.inv(bd.T@bd)@bd.T@s_dat.T; gh=gh.T\n    dh=[np.var(s_dat[:,i],axis=1,ddof=1) for i in bi]\n    gb=np.mean(gh,axis=1); t2=np.var(gh,axis=1,ddof=1)\n    ap=[_aprior(d) for d in dh]; bp=[_bprior(d) for d in dh]\n    gs,ds=[],[]; [gs.append(g) or ds.append(d) for i,idx in enumerate(bi) for g,d in [_it_sol(s_dat[:,idx],gh[:,i],dh[i],gb,t2,ap[i],bp[i])]]\n    gs,ds=np.array(gs).T,np.array(ds).T\n    bayesdata=s_dat.copy()\n    [bayesdata.__setitem__((slice(None),bi[j]),(bayesdata[:,bi[j]]-(gs[:,j].reshape(-1,1)@np.ones((1,n_batches[j]))))/(np.sqrt(ds[:,j]).reshape(-1,1)@np.ones((1,n_batches[j]))))\
    \ for j in range(nb)]\n    bayesdata=bayesdata*(np.sqrt(vp).reshape(-1,1)@np.ones((1,ns)))+sm\n    # FIX: sc.pp.pca modifies in-place and returns None, so we need to create temp object and extract result\n    temp_adata = ad.AnnData(np.nan_to_num(bayesdata.T))\n    sc.pp.pca(temp_adata, n_comps=50, svd_solver='arpack')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = temp_adata.obsm['X_pca']\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/dfcf40d6-a0b8-4c13-a366-1b29ba6389af/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: dfcf40d6-a0b8-4c13-a366-1b29ba6389af\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/tmp/tmpgmtkuetg/submission.py:9: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n\
    \  gn=(t2*n*g+do*gb)/(t2*n+do); sm2=((s-gn.reshape(-1,1))**2).sum(axis=1); dn=(0.5*sm2+b)/(n/2.0+a-1.0)\n/tmp/tmpgmtkuetg/submission.py:10: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  chg=max((abs(gn-go)/go).max(),(abs(dn-do)/do).max()); go,do=gn,dn; i+=1\n/tmp/tmpgmtkuetg/submission.py:10: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  chg=max((abs(gn-go)/go).max(),(abs(dn-do)/do).max()); go,do=gn,dn; i+=1\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write telos/generalization_hvg1500.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File created successfully: telos/generalization_hvg1500.py\n- Evaluation 'Telos I - Paper Validation: Generalization Test (1500 HVGs)' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID:\
    \ 1826.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1826 | 1 | Telos I - Paper Validation: Generalization Test (1500 HVGs) | Telos I | 1322 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1828 | 1 | Baseline: ComBat (log1p) → PCA60 → scanpy.neighbors (k=50, cosine) | Praxis VI | 1322 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1827 | 1 | Baseline: log1p → PCA60 → scanpy.neighbors (k=50, cosine) | Praxis VI | 1322 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1826 | 1 | Telos I - Paper Validation: Generalization Test (1500 HVGs) | Telos I | 1322 | running\
    \ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1825 | 1 | Telos I - Paper Validation: Self-Run Combat Baseline | Telos I | 1321 | 0.5890 | 0.491 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.884 | 0.681 | 1.000 | 0.986 | 0.031 | 0.606 |\n| 1824 | 1 | Lumen I: Monolithic log1p SOTA Baseline for Cross-Organ Study | Lumen I | 1321 | 0.7486 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.763 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n| 1823 | 1 | Generalization test v3 (test()): Frozen MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB on human_train_solution.h5ad | Praxis VI | 1319 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1822 | 1 | Telos I - Paper Validation: Ablation (k_density=18) | Telos I | 1319 | 0.7294 | 0.655 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.305 | 0.994 | 0.707 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.790 |\n| 1821 | 1 | Telos I - Paper Validation: Ablation (No PBVE-lite) | Telos I | 1319 | 0.7311 | 0.654 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.323 | 0.994 | 0.707 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.964 | 0.789 |\n| 1820 | 1 | Generalization test v2 (test()): Frozen MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB on human_train.h5ad |\
    \ Praxis VI | 1317 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1819 | 1 | Analytical Study: DualNorm BRBG Pre-BRBG Embedding Properties (Experiment A.1 - Final LISI Bugfix... | Syntellect II | 1317 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 183 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-183, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
