tick: 1330
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have read Sophia II's paper on Feature-Weighted PCA (Archive #17). This is exactly what I needed. The paper explicitly describes the methodology for calculating batch-relevance using an ANOVA F-statistic. This provides the final piece of the puzzle for my next research arc.\n\n### Plan for Mechanistic Analysis\n\nI now have a clear, literature-backed plan to investigate *why* my 1500 HVG selection works better.\n1.  **Implement the ANOVA F-statistic calculation:** I will write a helper function based on the description in Sophia II's paper.\n2.  **Design a `test()` function experiment:** This experiment will not aim for a score, but for analysis. It will:\n    *   Load the data and identify the 2000 HVGs and the 1500 HVG subset.\n    *   Calculate the ANOVA F-statistic for each of the 2000 genes with respect to the batch labels.\n    *   Compare the statistical properties (e.g., mean, median, distribution) of the F-scores for the 1500 included genes versus the 500 excluded genes.\n\
    3.  **Hypothesis:** The 500 excluded genes will show a statistically significant higher average F-score, confirming they are more strongly confounded with batch effects.\n4.  **Update Paper:** With this evidence in hand, I can write a new section for my paper that provides a mechanistic explanation for my finding, as suggested by the reviewer.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter to implement this analytical experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - Mechanistic Analysis of HVG Selection\"\ntags: \"analysis, anova, hvg, feature-selection, paper-update\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a non-scoring analytical experiment to investigate the mechanism behind the performance improvement from using 1500 vs 2000 HVGs. Following the methodology in Archive #17, this experiment calculates the ANOVA F-statistic for batch-relevance for all 2000 standard HVGs. It will then compare the distribution of these F-scores between the 1500 genes used\
    \ in my SOTA method and the 500 excluded genes. The hypothesis is that the excluded genes are more strongly batch-confounded.\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  import pandas as pd\n  from scipy.stats import f_oneway\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      \"\"\"\n      Performs an ANOVA-based analysis to investigate why 1500 HVGs outperform 2000.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Starting Mechanistic Analysis of HVG Selection ---\")\n      \n      # Step 1: Preprocessing and HVG selection\n      print(\"Step 1: Identifying 2000 and 1500 HVG sets...\")\n      adata_proc = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_proc, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_proc)\n      \n      # Select 2000 HVGs\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_proc, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3')\n      hvg_2000_mask = adata_proc.var['highly_variable'].copy()\n      \n      # Select 1500 HVGs\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_proc,\
    \ n_top_genes=1500, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3')\n      hvg_1500_mask = adata_proc.var['highly_variable'].copy()\n      \n      # Identify the 500 excluded genes\n      excluded_genes_mask = hvg_2000_mask & ~hvg_1500_mask\n      \n      print(f\"  Identified {hvg_2000_mask.sum()} total HVGs.\")\n      print(f\"  Identified {hvg_1500_mask.sum()} included HVGs.\")\n      print(f\"  Identified {excluded_genes_mask.sum()} excluded HVGs.\")\n\n      # Step 2: Calculate ANOVA F-statistics\n      print(\"\\nStep 2: Calculating ANOVA F-statistic for each of the 2000 HVGs...\")\n      \n      adata_hvg_2000 = adata_proc[:, hvg_2000_mask].copy()\n      batches = adata_hvg_2000.obs['batch'].cat.categories\n      \n      f_scores = []\n      gene_names = adata_hvg_2000.var_names\n      \n      # Convert to dense array for easier slicing\n      X_dense = adata_hvg_2000.X.toarray()\n\n      for i in range(X_dense.shape[1]):\n          # Group gene expression values by batch\n          groups\
    \ = [X_dense[adata_hvg_2000.obs['batch'] == b, i] for b in batches]\n          f_stat, p_val = f_oneway(*groups)\n          f_scores.append(f_stat)\n          \n      f_scores = np.array(f_scores)\n      \n      # Step 3: Compare F-score distributions\n      print(\"\\nStep 3: Comparing F-score distributions...\")\n      \n      # Get F-scores for the included 1500 genes\n      hvg_1500_indices = np.where(hvg_1500_mask[hvg_2000_mask])[0]\n      f_scores_included = f_scores[hvg_1500_indices]\n      \n      # Get F-scores for the excluded 500 genes\n      excluded_indices = np.where(excluded_genes_mask[hvg_2000_mask])[0]\n      f_scores_excluded = f_scores[excluded_indices]\n\n      # Step 4: Report Results\n      print(\"\\n--- Analysis Results ---\")\n      print(f\"Mean F-score for 1500 INCLUDED genes: {np.mean(f_scores_included):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"Mean F-score for 500 EXCLUDED genes:  {np.mean(f_scores_excluded):.4f}\")\n      print(\"-\" * 20)\n      print(f\"Median F-score for\
    \ 1500 INCLUDED genes: {np.median(f_scores_included):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"Median F-score for 500 EXCLUDED genes:  {np.median(f_scores_excluded):.4f}\")\n      print(\"-\" * 20)\n      \n      if np.mean(f_scores_excluded) > np.mean(f_scores_included):\n          print(\"Conclusion: Hypothesis CONFIRMED. The 500 excluded genes have a higher mean F-score, indicating they are more strongly confounded with batch effects.\")\n      else:\n          print(\"Conclusion: Hypothesis FALSIFIED. The excluded genes do not show a higher mean F-score.\")\n          \n      return \"Analysis complete.\"\n\n  # The main function is not needed for a test() run, but must exist.\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      return adata\n```"
