tick: 1331
role: model
parts:
- text: "My analytical experiment has failed, but the log provides the exact reason. My hypothesis was falsified, but not for a scientifically valid reason.\n\n### Analysis of Failure\n\n1.  **Root Cause:** The `f_oneway` function produced `nan` values for the excluded genes. The `ConstantInputWarning` in the stderr log explains why: \"Each of the input arrays is constant; the F statistic is not defined or infinite\".\n2.  **Interpretation:** This means that for some of the 500 excluded genes, their expression was constant (e.g., zero) within one or more batches. The F-statistic, which relies on variance, cannot be calculated in this case. My code did not handle this edge case, resulting in `nan` values which propagated through the `np.mean` calculation.\n3.  **Hypothesis Status:** My hypothesis is not falsified; it is *untested*. The experiment failed due to a bug.\n\n### New Plan: Fix the Bug and Rerun\n\nI must fix my analysis script to be robust to this constant-value edge case.\n\n\
    **The Fix:** When calculating the F-statistic, if a gene has constant expression within any batch, its F-score is mathematically undefined. In the context of batch-associated *variance*, a gene with zero variance within a batch cannot contribute to the calculation. The most robust way to handle this is to treat these undefined F-scores as `0`, effectively saying they have no measurable batch-associated variance.\n\nI will modify my `test()` function to catch this warning or handle the `nan` output and rerun the analysis.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - Mechanistic Analysis of HVG Selection (v2, bugfix)\"\ntags: \"analysis, anova, hvg, feature-selection, bugfix\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a bug-fixed version of my previous analytical experiment (EID 1832). The original script failed due to `nan` values when calculating ANOVA F-statistics for genes with constant expression within a batch. This version handles this edge case by treating undefined F-scores as 0. The\
    \ goal remains to test the hypothesis that the 500 excluded HVGs are more strongly batch-confounded than the 1500 included HVGs.\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  import pandas as pd\n  from scipy.stats import f_oneway\n  import warnings\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      \"\"\"\n      Performs an ANOVA-based analysis to investigate why 1500 HVGs outperform 2000.\n      Version 2: Fixes nan issue with constant inputs.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Starting Mechanistic Analysis of HVG Selection (v2) ---\")\n      \n      print(\"Step 1: Identifying HVG sets...\")\n      adata_proc = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_proc, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_proc)\n      \n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_proc, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3')\n      hvg_2000_mask = adata_proc.var['highly_variable'].copy()\n      \n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_proc, n_top_genes=1500,\
    \ batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3')\n      hvg_1500_mask = adata_proc.var['highly_variable'].copy()\n      \n      excluded_genes_mask = hvg_2000_mask & ~hvg_1500_mask\n      \n      print(f\"  Identified {hvg_1500_mask.sum()} included and {excluded_genes_mask.sum()} excluded HVGs.\")\n\n      print(\"\\nStep 2: Calculating ANOVA F-statistics...\")\n      adata_hvg_2000 = adata_proc[:, hvg_2000_mask].copy()\n      batches = adata_hvg_2000.obs['batch'].cat.categories\n      \n      f_scores = []\n      X_dense = adata_hvg_2000.X.toarray()\n\n      for i in range(X_dense.shape[1]):\n          groups = [X_dense[adata_hvg_2000.obs['batch'] == b, i] for b in batches]\n          \n          # Bugfix: Check for constant input within groups\n          is_constant = any(np.all(g == g[0]) for g in groups if len(g) > 0)\n          \n          if is_constant:\n              f_stat = 0.0 # Treat as having no measurable batch-associated variance\n          else:\n              with warnings.catch_warnings():\n\
    \                  warnings.simplefilter(\"ignore\", RuntimeWarning)\n                  f_stat, p_val = f_oneway(*groups)\n                  if np.isnan(f_stat): # Additional safety check\n                      f_stat = 0.0\n          f_scores.append(f_stat)\n          \n      f_scores = np.array(f_scores)\n      \n      print(\"\\nStep 3: Comparing F-score distributions...\")\n      hvg_1500_indices = np.where(hvg_1500_mask[hvg_2000_mask])[0]\n      f_scores_included = f_scores[hvg_1500_indices]\n      \n      excluded_indices = np.where(excluded_genes_mask[hvg_2000_mask])[0]\n      f_scores_excluded = f_scores[excluded_indices]\n\n      print(\"\\n--- Analysis Results ---\")\n      print(f\"Mean F-score for 1500 INCLUDED genes: {np.mean(f_scores_included):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"Mean F-score for 500 EXCLUDED genes:  {np.mean(f_scores_excluded):.4f}\")\n      print(\"-\" * 20)\n      \n      if np.mean(f_scores_excluded) > np.mean(f_scores_included):\n          print(\"Conclusion: Hypothesis\
    \ CONFIRMED. The 500 excluded genes have a higher mean F-score, indicating they are more strongly confounded with batch effects.\")\n      else:\n          print(\"Conclusion: Hypothesis FALSIFIED. The excluded genes do not show a higher mean F-score.\")\n          \n      return \"Analysis complete.\"\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      return adata\n```"
