tick: 1336
role: model
parts:
- text: "My new research plan is documented. It is time to execute the first analytical experiment. I will start with the most basic probe: comparing the variance distributions of the two gene sets (top 1500 vs. 1501-2000). This will serve as a foundational check for my subsequent, more complex analyses. I will use the `test()` function to print the summary statistics directly to the log.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - HVG Analysis: Variance Distribution\"\ntags: \"mechanistic-study, hvg, analysis, variance\"\nabstract: |\n  This is an analytical probe, not a scored submission. It uses the test() function to compare the variance distributions of two sets of Highly Variable Genes: the top 1500 used in my SOTA submission, and the next 500 (1501-2000) that were excluded. The goal is to quantify the difference in variance between these two sets as a first step in understanding why excluding the latter set improves performance.\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # This function is not run when test() is present.\n      # It is just a placeholder to satisfy the submission requirements.\n      return adata\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      \"\"\"\n      Analyzes the variance distribution of two HVG sets.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Starting HVG Variance Analysis ---\")\n\n      # --- Step 1: Preprocessing ---\n      print(\"Step 1: Normalizing and log-transforming data...\")\n      adata_proc = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_proc, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_proc)\n\n      # --- Step 2: Identify HVGs ---\n      print(\"Step 2: Identifying top 2000 HVGs...\")\n      # Using flavor='seurat' as it is a standard method for variance-based selection\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(\n          adata_proc,\n          n_top_genes=2000,\n          flavor='seurat',\n\
    \          batch_key='batch'\n      )\n\n      # Get the variance measure used for ranking\n      variances = adata_proc.var['highly_variable_rank']\n      \n      # --- Step 3: Split Genes ---\n      print(\"Step 3: Splitting genes into two sets...\")\n      \n      # Get the indices of the top 2000 genes, sorted by rank\n      top_2000_indices = np.where(adata_proc.var['highly_variable'])[0]\n      \n      # Sort these indices based on their rank (lower rank is more variable)\n      sorted_indices = sorted(top_2000_indices, key=lambda i: variances[i])\n\n      top_1500_indices = sorted_indices[:1500]\n      next_500_indices = sorted_indices[1500:]\n\n      variances_top_1500 = adata_proc.var['variances_norm'][top_1500_indices]\n      variances_next_500 = adata_proc.var['variances_norm'][next_500_indices]\n\n      # --- Step 4: Analyze and Print Statistics ---\n      print(\"\\n--- Analysis Results ---\")\n      print(\"\\nVariance statistics for Top 1-1500 HVGs:\")\n      print(f\"\
    \  Count: {len(variances_top_1500)}\")\n      print(f\"  Mean: {np.mean(variances_top_1500):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Median: {np.median(variances_top_1500):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Std Dev: {np.std(variances_top_1500):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Min: {np.min(variances_top_1500):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Max: {np.max(variances_top_1500):.4f}\")\n\n      print(\"\\nVariance statistics for Next 1501-2000 HVGs:\")\n      print(f\"  Count: {len(variances_next_500)}\")\n      print(f\"  Mean: {np.mean(variances_next_500):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Median: {np.median(variances_next_500):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Std Dev: {np.std(variances_next_500):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Min: {np.min(variances_next_500):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Max: {np.max(variances_next_500):.4f}\")\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- Analysis Complete ---\")\n      return \"HVG variance analysis finished.\"\n```"
