parts:
- text: "My analytical probe has failed with a `KeyError: 'highly_variable_rank'`.\n\n### Analysis of Failure\n\nThe error is simple: `sc.pp.highly_variable_genes` with `flavor='seurat'` does not populate the `adata.var['highly_variable_rank']` column. That column is populated by `flavor='seurat_v3'`, which is what the SOTA pipeline uses. I used the wrong `flavor` in my test script.\n\nThis is a straightforward bug to fix. I will correct the `flavor` parameter and resubmit the analysis.\n\n### Plan\n\nI will correct the script and resubmit immediately. I am confident this fix will work.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - HVG Analysis: Variance Distribution (v2, bugfix)\"\ntags: \"mechanistic-study, hvg, analysis, variance, bugfix\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a bugfix for submission 1838. The previous version used the wrong `flavor` in `sc.pp.highly_variable_genes`, causing a KeyError. This version corrects the flavor to 'seurat_v3' to match the SOTA pipeline. The goal\
    \ remains to compare the variance distributions of the top 1500 HVGs vs. the next 500.\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  import pandas as pd\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      return adata\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      \"\"\"\n      Analyzes the variance distribution of two HVG sets.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Starting HVG Variance Analysis (v2, bugfix) ---\")\n\n      # --- Step 1: Preprocessing ---\n      print(\"Step 1: Normalizing and log-transforming data...\")\n      adata_proc = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_proc, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_proc)\n\n      # --- Step 2: Identify HVGs ---\n      print(\"Step 2: Identifying top 2000 HVGs using flavor='seurat_v3'...\")\n      # FIX: Use 'seurat_v3' to match the SOTA pipeline and get the correct rank column\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(\n          adata_proc,\n          n_top_genes=2000,\n\
    \          flavor='seurat_v3',\n          batch_key='batch'\n      )\n\n      # Get the ranking values\n      ranks = adata_proc.var['highly_variable_rank']\n      \n      # --- Step 3: Split Genes ---\n      print(\"Step 3: Splitting genes into two sets based on rank...\")\n      \n      # Get indices of all HVGs\n      hvg_indices = np.where(adata_proc.var['highly_variable'])[0]\n      \n      # Sort indices by rank\n      sorted_hvg_indices = sorted(hvg_indices, key=lambda i: ranks[i])\n      \n      top_1500_indices = sorted_hvg_indices[:1500]\n      next_500_indices = sorted_hvg_indices[1500:]\n\n      # The 'variances_norm' is also specific to seurat_v3 flavor\n      variances_top_1500 = adata_proc.var['variances_norm'][top_1500_indices]\n      variances_next_500 = adata_proc.var['variances_norm'][next_500_indices]\n\n      # --- Step 4: Analyze and Print Statistics ---\n      print(\"\\n--- Analysis Results ---\")\n      print(\"\\nNormalized variance statistics for Top 1-1500\
    \ HVGs:\")\n      print(f\"  Count: {len(variances_top_1500)}\")\n      print(f\"  Mean: {np.mean(variances_top_1500):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Median: {np.median(variances_top_1500):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Std Dev: {np.std(variances_top_1500):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Min: {np.min(variances_top_1500):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Max: {np.max(variances_top_1500):.4f}\")\n\n      print(\"\\nNormalized variance statistics for Next 1501-2000 HVGs:\")\n      print(f\"  Count: {len(variances_next_500)}\")\n      print(f\"  Mean: {np.mean(variances_next_500):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Median: {np.median(variances_next_500):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Std Dev: {np.std(variances_next_500):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Min: {np.min(variances_next_500):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Max: {np.max(variances_next_500):.4f}\")\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- Analysis Complete ---\")\n      return \"HVG variance analysis finished successfully.\"\n```"
