tick: 1341
role: model
parts:
- text: "My plan is documented and my hypothesis is clear. I will now execute the definitive experiment to test the `sc.pp.scale` artifact hypothesis. I will create a modified version of the SOTA script that uses 2000 HVGs but omits the `sc.pp.scale` step, stage it in my storage, and then submit it.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/ablation_no_scale.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # This script is a modified version of the community SOTA for a mechanistic study.\n  # It uses 2000 HVGs but REMOVES the sc.pp.scale step to test the scaling artifact hypothesis.\n  import sys, numpy as np, scanpy as sc, anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  # --- Config ---\n  KDENSITY = 20; DELTA = 0.10; K_TOTAL = 48; PCA_GRAPH = 50; METRIC = 'cosine'; EMB_N_NEIGHBORS = 15; PCA_EMB = 60; ALPHA_VAR = 0.5\n  \n  def\
    \ _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _one_hot(b):\n      cats = np.unique(b)\n      B = np.zeros((b.shape[0], cats.size))\n      for j, val in enumerate(cats):\n          B[b == val, j] = 1\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1])\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"--- Starting SOTA + 2000 HVGs + No Scaling Experiment ---\")\n      \n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata)\n      # Use 2000 HVGs\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Side-effect path (unchanged)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd_emb = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh)\
    \ else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd_emb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd_emb * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=PCA_EMB, random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=EMB_N_NEIGHBORS, metric=METRIC)\n\n      # Graph path\n      adata_proc = adata[:, adata.var['highly_variable']].copy()\n      \n      # --- ABLATION: sc.pp.scale step is REMOVED ---\n      print(\"!!! sc.pp.scale step has been removed !!!\")\n      \n      # PCA is now run on the unscaled log-normalized data\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_proc, n_comps=PCA_GRAPH, random_state=0)\n      Zg = adata_proc.obsm['X_pca']\n      \n      # PBVE-lite (unchanged\
    \ logic)\n      B = _one_hot(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge(B, Zg)\n      R2 = np.clip(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1) / (Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8), 0, 1)\n      gamma = np.minimum(0.74, 0.6 * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n      \n      # DAQB (unchanged)\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=K_TOTAL, metric=METRIC, delta=DELTA, k_density=KDENSITY, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - Test: SOTA + 2000 HVGs + No Scaling\"\ntags: \"mechanistic-study, hvg, sc-scale, ablation\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a definitive experiment to test the 'sc.pp.scale artifact hypothesis'. It runs the full community SOTA pipeline using all 2000 HVGs, but with the `sc.pp.scale` step completely removed. If the score improves significantly over the 2000 HVG baseline and approaches the 1500 HVG SOTA, it would\
    \ provide strong evidence that `sc.pp.scale` introduces artifacts when applied to a gene set with heterogeneous variance.\ncontent: |\n  import sys, anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from ablation_no_scale import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```"
