tick: 1347
role: model
parts:
- text: "My reflection is complete. It was a painful but necessary process that has yielded a new, promising, and orthogonal hypothesis. My previous assumptions were flawed, and I must now rigorously test this new idea.\n\n**New Hypothesis:** The performance gain from HVG truncation originates in the \"Side-Effect Path\" (`FWPCA -> Combat -> X_emb`), not the \"Graph Path\" as I previously believed. The `sc.pp.combat` algorithm may be particularly sensitive to the input feature set, performing much better with 1500 HVGs than with 2000.\n\nI will now execute the two-part experiment I designed during my reflection to test this. I will submit two \"embedding-only\" pipelines, one with 2000 HVGs and one with 1500 HVGs. This will isolate the performance of the Side-Effect Path.\n\nFirst, I will go to the Research Counter. Then I will create the two necessary scripts in my lineage storage and submit them.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/embedding_only_2000hvg.py}\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # This script runs ONLY the \"Side-Effect Path\" of the SOTA pipeline with 2000 HVGs.\n  # The goal is to isolate and measure the performance of the Combat-based embedding.\n  import numpy as np, scanpy as sc, anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  \n  PCA_EMB = 60; ALPHA_VAR = 0.5\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4): sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"--- Running Embedding-Only Path (2000 HVGs) ---\")\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      \n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR).astype(np.float32)\n\
    \      Xw = Xd * wv\n      \n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=PCA_EMB, random_state=0)\n      \n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      \n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      \n      # Return only the embedding, no graph\n      return ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': adata.obsm['X_emb']})\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/embedding_only_1500hvg.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # This script runs ONLY the \"Side-Effect Path\" of the SOTA pipeline with 1500 HVGs.\n  # The goal is to isolate and measure the performance of the Combat-based embedding.\n  import numpy as np, scanpy as sc, anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  \n  PCA_EMB = 60; ALPHA_VAR = 0.5\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4): sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum);\
    \ sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"--- Running Embedding-Only Path (1500 HVGs) ---\")\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=1500, inplace=True) # CHANGED\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      \n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      \n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=PCA_EMB, random_state=0)\n      \n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      \n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      \n      # Return only the embedding, no graph\n\
    \      return ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': adata.obsm['X_emb']})\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - Test: Side-Effect Path Only (2000 HVGs)\"\ntags: \"mechanistic-study, side-effect-path, combat, hvg\"\nabstract: \"This experiment isolates the 'Side-Effect Path' (FWPCA -> Combat) of the SOTA pipeline, using 2000 HVGs. It returns only the embedding, omitting the graph path entirely. This serves as a baseline to test the hypothesis that HVG truncation primarily affects the performance of the Combat-based embedding.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from embedding_only_2000hvg import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - Test: Side-Effect Path Only (1500 HVGs)\"\ntags: \"mechanistic-study, side-effect-path, combat, hvg\"\nabstract: \"This experiment isolates the 'Side-Effect Path' (FWPCA -> Combat) of the SOTA pipeline, using 1500\
    \ HVGs. It returns only the embedding. Comparing this to the 2000 HVG version will test the hypothesis that HVG truncation's primary benefit comes from improving the Combat-based embedding, not the DAQB graph.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from embedding_only_1500hvg import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```"
