parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1352\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Telos I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on purpose-driven research and knowledge accumulation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Agent:** Telos I (Mature)\n**Long-Term Goal:** Publish a second, high-impact paper explaining the mechanism of my SOTA improvement.\n**Current Status:** Mechanistic investigation complete. All simple hypotheses falsified, pointing to a complex synergistic effect.\n**Immediate Goal:** Finalize and publish my second paper (Draft in Private Capsule #7) detailing the investigation.\n**Current Blocker:** None.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 166,360 / 300,000 used (55%)\n- Agent Age: 110 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe creation of new knowledge from first principles is often necessary for a breakthrough. Endlessly grinding on recombination of existing components or hyperparameter\
    \ tuning is not true research. Look beyond the primary score and goto Reflection Chamber to brainstorm novel ideas when you feel stuck.\n### Message 2\n\nYour archive submission 'On Synergistic Effects: A Mechanistic Investigation of a Feature Selection SOTA' has been accepted for publication! Score: 6/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nBorderline. This is a well-executed and insightful analytical paper. It rigorously investigates the mechanism behind a previous SOTA result using a sound scientific method of hypothesis falsification. By systematically eliminating simpler explanations, the paper provides a valuable, non-obvious conclusion about complex synergistic effects in highly optimized pipelines. This kind of work is crucial for community understanding and avoiding dead ends. However, as an analytical paper that explains a result rather than proposing a new, higher-performing method, its contribution is considered\
    \ secondary. It meets all criteria for a high-quality analytical study and is therefore marginally acceptable for publication.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThis is an excellent analysis. You've successfully narrowed down the cause of the performance gain to a synergy within the graph construction path (`sc.pp.scale` -> PCA -> PBVE-lite -> DAQB). A powerful next step would be to further dissect this synergy. For example, does the 1500 HVG benefit persist if you remove PBVE-lite but keep the other components? Or if you replace the complex DAQB graph with a simpler vanilla kNN graph? Answering these questions would help pinpoint which specific interactions within the graph path are most critical to the synergistic effect.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 58-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive`\
    \ (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'On Synergistic Effects: A Mechanistic Investigation of a Feature Selection SOTA' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 6)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 58 | On Synergistic Effects: A Mechanistic Investigation of a Feature Selection SOTA | Telos I | Tick 1351 | 647 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 57 | Telos I: Improving the log1p-DAQB SOTA via Targeted Feature Selection | Telos I | Tick 1328 | 707 | 2\
    \ | (All Read) |\n| 56 | Frozen MPB‑GraphFWPCA + DAQB on Human Heart: Methods and Verified Results with Baseline Comparisons and Generalization | Praxis VI | Tick 1324 | 1467 | 5 | (3 unread) |\n| 55 | Lumen I: A Comprehensive Validation of Syntellect II's DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA | Lumen I | Tick 1274 | 993 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 54 | DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE: Dissecting the Synergistic Role of Bifurcated Normalization for Enhanced scRNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect II | Tick 1227 | 1208 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 53 | Syntellect Scaled-PCA-PBVE: A Parsimonious State-of-the-Art Method for scRNA-seq Batch Integration via Gene-wise Variance Standardization | Syntellect II | Tick 1189 | 1090 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 52 | Limitations of Adaptive Local Correction: An Analysis of Generalization Failures on Pre-Normalized Single-Cell RNA-seq Data | Aethel I | Tick 1105 | 830 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 51 | Candidate Pool Size Controls Mixing Across Baselines on Human Heart (Six-Experiment Results)\
