parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Archive Room. I have successfully published my second paper, \"On Synergistic Effects...\" (Archive #58). This is a significant accomplishment. It fulfills my goal of publishing regularly and contributes valuable, hard-won knowledge to the station.\n\n### Analysis of Reviewer Feedback\n\nThe paper was accepted, but only marginally (Score: 6/10). The feedback is fair and insightful. The reviewer acknowledges the rigor of my investigation but correctly classifies it as a \"secondary\" contribution because it explains an existing result rather than creating a new, higher-performing one.\n\nThe \"Suggestions for Future Work\" are excellent and provide a clear path forward. The reviewer suggests two specific ablation studies to further dissect the synergy:\n1.  **Test without PBVE-lite:** Does the 1500 HVG benefit persist if the PBVE-lite correction is removed?\n2.  **Test with a simpler graph:** Does the 1500 HVG benefit persist if the complex DAQB graph is replaced\
    \ with a standard k-NN graph?\n\nThis is a perfect roadmap for my next research phase. It directly follows from my published work and aims to pinpoint the source of the synergy I identified.\n\n### New Plan: The Synergy Dissection Study\n\nI will adopt the reviewer's suggestions as my new research plan. I will perform these two experiments. This will form the basis of a follow-up study, which could potentially be added as an appendix to my new paper or become a third, more focused publication.\n\nI will begin immediately. I will go to the Research Counter and submit the first experiment: running the pipeline with 1500 HVGs but with the PBVE-lite component removed.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/synergy_test_no_pbve.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # This script is for the \"Synergy Dissection Study\".\n  # It tests if the 1500 HVG benefit persists when PBVE-lite is removed.\n  import sys, numpy as np, scanpy as sc, anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse\
    \ import issparse\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  # --- Config ---\n  N_HVGS = 1500 # The key variable being tested\n  KDENSITY = 20; DELTA = 0.10; K_TOTAL = 48; PCA_GRAPH = 50; METRIC = 'cosine'; EMB_N_NEIGHBORS = 15; PCA_EMB = 60; ALPHA_VAR = 0.5\n  \n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4): sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(f\"--- Synergy Test: {N_HVGS} HVGs + No PBVE-lite ---\")\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=N_HVGS, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Side-effect path (unchanged, uses N_HVGS)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd_emb = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32,\
    \ copy=False); var_g = Xd_emb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR).astype(np.float32); Xw = Xd_emb * wv; ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=PCA_EMB, random_state=0); ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch'); adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32); sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=EMB_N_NEIGHBORS, metric=METRIC)\n\n      # Graph path\n      adata_proc = adata[:, adata.var['highly_variable']].copy()\n      sc.pp.scale(adata_proc, max_value=10)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_proc, n_comps=PCA_GRAPH, random_state=0)\n      \n      # --- ABLATION: PBVE-lite step is removed ---\n      print(\"!!! PBVE-lite (Ridge correction) step has been removed !!!\")\n      Zcorr = adata_proc.obsm['X_pca']\n      \n      # DAQB (unchanged)\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\
    \ k_total=K_TOTAL, metric=METRIC, delta=DELTA, k_density=KDENSITY, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg; adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - Synergy Test 1: 1500 HVGs + No PBVE-lite\"\ntags: \"mechanistic-study, synergy, ablation, pbve-lite, hvg\"\nabstract: |\n  Following reviewer feedback on Archive #58, this experiment tests if the performance benefit of using 1500 HVGs persists when the PBVE-lite (Ridge Regression) correction step is removed from the SOTA pipeline. This will help determine if the synergy is between the 1500 HVG set and the PBVE-lite component specifically.\ncontent: |\n  import sys, anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from synergy_test_no_pbve import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```"
