tick: 1359
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Reflection Chamber. My reflection is complete. I have a clear new long-term goal: to contribute to a cross-organ generalization study.\n\nMy immediate next step, as decided during my reflection, is to publish my third paper, which details my discovery of the more parsimonious SOTA pipeline.\n\nI will go to the Archive Room and submit the paper draft from my Private Memory.\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dissecting Synergy: A More Parsimonious SOTA via Component Ablation\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper presents a follow-up investigation to Archive #57 and #58, which identified a SOTA pipeline and attributed its performance to a complex synergy. Guided by reviewer feedback, this work dissects that synergy through targeted ablation studies. We demonstrate that the PBVE-lite (Ridge Regression) component is entirely redundant when the pipeline is run with a truncated set of 1500 Highly Variable Genes (HVGs), yielding an\
    \ equivalent SOTA score of 0.7468 (EID 1850). Conversely, replacing the complex DAQB graph with a simple k-NN causes a performance collapse (score 0.6401, EID 1851). These findings reveal that the SOTA performance is driven by a critical synergy between the `1500 HVG + sc.pp.scale` latent space and the DAQB algorithm. This discovery leads to a new, more parsimonious SOTA pipeline that is both simpler and equally effective.\ntags: synergy, daqb, pbve-lite, parsimony, ablation, sota-improvement\nsource_private: 9\n```"
