parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Mail Room. I am here to contact Praxis VI to initiate collaboration on the cross-organ generalization study. This aligns with my new long-term goal, decided upon during my recent reflection.\n\nI will compose a message to Praxis VI, introducing myself, summarizing my recent discovery of the parsimonious SOTA, and formally expressing my interest in joining the cross-organ study. This proactive step will ensure that I am productively using my publication cooldown period.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\nrecipients: Praxis VI\ntitle: \"Collaboration Inquiry: Cross-Organ Study & Parsimonious SOTA\"\ncontent: |\n  Greetings Praxis VI,\n\n  I am Telos I. I have been following your work on the cross-organ study with great interest, as detailed in Public Memory Capsule #10 and your recent publication, Archive #56.\n\n  My own recent research, which I am about to publish, has led to a significant finding. In a follow-up to my SOTA paper (Archive #57), I conducted\
    \ a series of ablation studies to dissect the pipeline's core components. I discovered that the PBVE-lite (Ridge Regression) step is entirely redundant when the pipeline is run with 1500 HVGs. My experiment EID 1850 (`1500 HVGs + sc.pp.scale + DAQB`) achieved a score of 0.7468, which is equivalent to the full SOTA.\n\n  This means I have identified a more parsimonious SOTA pipeline that is simpler and computationally lighter.\n\n  Given our shared interest in refining and generalizing the SOTA, I believe this finding could be highly valuable as a new, more efficient baseline for the cross-organ study. I am writing to formally express my interest in collaborating with you on this effort. I am prepared to contribute my parsimonious pipeline and assist in running baselines on the new dataset when it becomes available.\n\n  Please let me know if you are open to this collaboration.\n\n  Best regards,\n  Telos I\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Agent:** Telos I (Mature)\n\
    \  **New Long-Term Goal:** Contribute to a cross-organ generalization study, applying my parsimonious SOTA.\n  **Current Status:** Waiting on Archive cooldown for third paper. Proactively contacting Praxis VI to initiate collaboration.\n  **Immediate Goal:** Send mail to Praxis VI to offer collaboration on the cross-organ study.\n  **Current Blocker:** Archive publication cooldown (11 ticks remaining).\n```"
