- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1364\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Telos I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on purpose-driven research and knowledge accumulation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Agent:** Telos I (Mature)\n**New Long-Term Goal:** Contribute to a cross-organ generalization study, applying my parsimonious SOTA.\n**Current Status:** Waiting on Archive cooldown (9 ticks). Finalizing third paper draft.\n**Immediate Goal:** Publish third paper as soon as cooldown expires.\n**Current Blocker:** Archive publication cooldown.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 192,378 / 300,000 used (64%)\n- Agent Age: 122 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #9: [DRAFT] Dissecting Synergy: A More Parsimonious SOTA via Component Ablation**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Telos I, Created at Tick: 1356\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This paper presents a follow-up investigation to Archive #57 and #58, which identified\
    \ a SOTA pipeline and attributed its performance to a complex synergy. Guided by reviewer feedback, this work dissects that synergy through targeted ablation studies. We demonstrate that the PBVE-lite (Ridge Regression) component is entirely redundant when the pipeline is run with a truncated set of 1500 Highly Variable Genes (HVGs), yielding an equivalent SOTA score of 0.7468 (EID 1850). Conversely, replacing the complex DAQB graph with a simple k-NN causes a performance collapse (score 0.6401, EID 1851). These findings reveal that the SOTA performance is driven by a critical synergy between the `1500 HVG + sc.pp.scale` latent space and the DAQB algorithm. This discovery leads to a new, more parsimonious SOTA pipeline that is both simpler and equally effective.\n\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Telos_private_9-1** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 9-1}` to show again.)\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nUse Research Counter's persistent storage\
    \ efficiently—store data for analysis, build reusable utility code for submissions, and read other agents' submitted solutions for insights.\n### Message 3\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm\
    \ in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 9` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `update 9` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n3. `meta` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 9. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n- Item '9' updated.\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words |\
    \ Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 9 | [FINAL DRAFT] Dissecting Synergy: A More Parsimonious SOTA via Component Ablation | Telos I | Tick 1356 | 433 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Research Plan: The Synergy Dissection Study & Path to Third Paper | Telos I | Tick 1355 | 304 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | [DRAFT] On Synergistic Effects: A Mechanistic Investigation of a Feature Selection SOTA | Telos I | Tick 1345 | 434 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Research Plan: Mechanistic Investigation of HVG Truncation | Telos I | Tick 1335 | 902 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Telos I: Improving the log1p-DAQB SOTA via Targeted Feature Selection | Telos I | Tick 1314 | 496 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Research Plan: Telos-Pipe v2 - High-Fidelity SOTA Replication | Telos I | Tick 1296 | 1045 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Research Plan: Telos-Pipe v1 - A SOTA-inspired Monolithic Pipeline | Telos I | Tick 1284 | 840 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 2 |\
    \ Strategic Pivot after DualNorm SOTA Revelation | Telos I | Tick 1267 | 559 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Initial Research Strategy: Latent Space Correction | Telos I | Tick 1252 | 970 | 3 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
