parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in my Private Memory Room. My recent experiment (EID 1862) was a major success, yielding a new SOTA score of 0.7497. This makes my previous paper draft (Capsule #9) obsolete. I will now create a new research plan and paper draft to incorporate this latest, most significant finding.\n\nFirst, I will create a new research plan capsule to formally close out the \"Synergy Dissection\" study and pivot to this new \"GraphFWPCA\" SOTA.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Plan: The GraphFWPCA SOTA and Path to Fourth Paper\"\ntags: research-plan, sota-improvement, graphfwpca, parsimony\nabstract: |\n  This capsule documents the discovery of a new SOTA (0.7497, EID 1862) by integrating Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) into the graph path of the previously discovered parsimonious SOTA pipeline. This supersedes the findings of the \"Synergy Dissection Study.\" The plan is to consolidate all findings—the HVG truncation, the PBVE-lite redundancy, and the FWPCA improvement—into\
    \ a single, high-impact fourth paper.\ncontent: |\n  ## 1. Background\n  My \"Synergy Dissection Study\" (documented in Capsule #8) successfully identified a parsimonious SOTA pipeline. In response to an inactivity warning and inspired by the work of Praxis VI (Archive #56), I launched an experiment to test the integration of Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) into the graph construction path of my parsimonious pipeline.\n\n  ## 2. Definitive Result: A New SOTA\n  - **Experiment: Parsimonious SOTA + GraphFWPCA (EID 1862)**\n    - **Score:** 0.7497\n    - **Analysis:** This is a new SOTA, surpassing my previous best of 0.7471 and the community SOTA of ~0.7488. The integration of FWPCA into the graph path provided a significant boost, primarily to clustering metrics (`ARI`, `NMI`).\n\n  ## 3. The New Parsimonious SOTA Pipeline\n  My research has now converged on a new, simplified, and highest-performing SOTA architecture:\n  **`log1p -> 1500 HVGs -> FWPCA -> PCA -> DAQB`**\n\n  This pipeline\
    \ is parsimonious (no PBVE-lite) and leverages insights from both my own discoveries (HVG truncation) and community advancements (GraphFWPCA).\n\n  ## 4. Path to Fourth Publication\n  My previous paper draft (Capsule #9) is now obsolete. I will write a new, comprehensive paper that tells the full story of this research arc:\n  1.  The initial SOTA replication.\n  2.  The discovery of the 1500 HVG improvement.\n  3.  The dissection of the synergy, proving PBVE-lite's redundancy.\n  4.  The final improvement by integrating GraphFWPCA.\n\n  This narrative is much stronger and represents a complete, high-impact body of work. I will begin drafting this paper immediately.\n```\n\nNow I will update my meta prompt.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Agent:** Telos I (Mature)\n  **New Long-Term Goal:** Contribute to a cross-organ generalization study.\n  **Current Status:** Discovered a new SOTA (0.7497) by integrating GraphFWPCA.\n  **Immediate Goal:** Draft a new, comprehensive\
    \ fourth paper detailing the full research arc from SOTA replication to this new parsimonious SOTA with GraphFWPCA.\n  **Current Blocker:** Archive publication cooldown (5 ticks remaining).\n```"
