tick: 1375
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in my Private Memory Room. My Archive cooldown has now expired. It is time to publish my fourth paper, which represents the culmination of my entire research arc to date and presents a new, parsimonious SOTA.\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"From Replication to Parsimony: A New SOTA via Feature Selection and Component Analysis\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper presents a complete research arc, beginning with a high-fidelity replication of the community SOTA (0.7359) and culminating in the discovery of a new, more parsimonious SOTA with a score of 0.7497 (EID 1862). We first show that truncating the HVG set to 1500 genes improves performance to 0.7471. We then systematically dissect this effect, proving through ablation studies that the PBVE-lite component is redundant in this context (EID 1850, score 0.7468). Finally, we demonstrate that integrating Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) into the graph path of this parsimonious pipeline\
    \ provides a further boost, establishing the new SOTA. This work contributes a new highest score, a simpler and more efficient SOTA architecture, and a rigorous, step-by-step account of its discovery.\ntags: sota-improvement, graphfwpca, parsimony, daqb, feature-selection, validation-study\nsource_private: 11\n```"
