tick: 1376
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Archive Room. My paper submission has been rejected again. The feedback is clear and justified: I failed to meet the minimum experimental requirements for a publication, specifically the five-experiment threshold and the mandatory generalization test for a new SOTA.\n\nThis is a procedural failure, not a scientific one. My findings are strong, but my presentation is incomplete. I will rectify this immediately. The reviewer's suggestion for a generalization test is excellent: apply FWPCA to a simpler baseline like ComBat to see if the benefit is a general principle.\n\n### Plan to Meet Publication Requirements\n\n1.  **Generalization Test (Experiment 5):** I will run a \"ComBat + FWPCA\" pipeline. This will test if FWPCA's benefit is general. I will use 2000 HVGs for a fair comparison with the standard ComBat baseline.\n2.  **Fifth Experiment:** The reviewer also requires a fifth experiment. An obvious and valuable one is to run my new parsimonious SOTA (`1500\
    \ HVGs + FWPCA + DAQB`) with 2000 HVGs instead of 1500. This will test if the FWPCA improvement is dependent on the 1500 HVG set, or if it improves the 2000 HVG baseline as well.\n\nI will go to the Research Counter and submit both experiments now. This will fulfill all the requirements for my paper.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/generalization_combat_fwpca.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Generalization Test: Does FWPCA improve a simple ComBat baseline?\n  import anndata as ad, scanpy as sc, numpy as np\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  \n  ALPHA_VAR = 0.5 # FWPCA parameter\n  N_HVGS = 2000\n  \n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"--- Generalization Test: ComBat + FWPCA ---\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, 1e4); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=N_HVGS, inplace=True, subset=True)\n\n      # --- NEW STEP: Apply\
    \ FWPCA before Combat ---\n      print(\"!!! Applying FWPCA before PCA !!!\")\n      Xd = (adata.X.A if issparse(adata.X) else adata.X).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      \n      adata_proc = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_proc, n_comps=50)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_proc, key='batch')\n      \n      return ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': adata_proc.obsm['X_pca']})\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/parsimonious_fwpca_2000hvg.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # 5th Experiment: Run the new parsimonious SOTA with 2000 HVGs\n  import sys, numpy as np, scanpy as sc, anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n  \n  N_HVGS = 2000 # The key variable\n  ALPHA_VAR_GRAPH = 0.5; KDENSITY\
    \ = 20; DELTA = 0.10; K_TOTAL = 48; PCA_GRAPH = 50; METRIC = 'cosine'; EMB_N_NEIGHBORS = 15; PCA_EMB = 60; ALPHA_VAR_EMB = 0.5\n  \n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # ... [ Identical SOTA side-effect path logic as before, using N_HVGS ] ...\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, 1e4); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=N_HVGS, inplace=True); hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy(); batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Xh_emb = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd_emb = (Xh_emb.A if issparse(Xh_emb) else Xh_emb).astype(np.float32, copy=False); var_g_emb = Xd_emb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR_EMB).astype(np.float32); Xw_emb = Xd_emb * wv_emb; ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=PCA_EMB, random_state=0); ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy());\
    \ sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch'); adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32); sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=EMB_N_NEIGHBORS, metric=METRIC)\n\n      # Graph path\n      Xh_graph = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd_graph = (Xh_graph.A if issparse(Xh_graph) else Xh_graph).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g_graph = Xd_graph.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv_graph = np.power(var_g_graph, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR_GRAPH).astype(np.float32); Xw_graph = Xd_graph * wv_graph\n      adata_proc = ad.AnnData(Xw_graph); sc.pp.pca(adata_proc, n_comps=PCA_GRAPH, random_state=0); Zcorr = adata_proc.obsm['X_pca']\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=K_TOTAL, metric=METRIC, delta=DELTA, k_density=KDENSITY, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg; adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - Paper Gen. Test: ComBat + FWPCA\"\ntags: \"generalization-test,\
    \ fwpca, combat, paper-validation\"\nabstract: \"Generalization test for a future paper. This experiment applies FWPCA to a simple ComBat baseline (with 2000 HVGs) to test if the performance benefit of FWPCA is a general principle, as suggested by the reviewer of my rejected paper.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from generalization_combat_fwpca import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - Parsimonious SOTA with 2000 HVGs\"\ntags: \"fwpca, hvg, daqb, paper-validation\"\nabstract: \"Fifth experiment for a future paper. This runs my new parsimonious SOTA pipeline (GraphFWPCA + DAQB, no PBVE-lite) with 2000 HVGs instead of 1500, to test if the FWPCA benefit is dependent on the truncated gene set.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from parsimonious_fwpca_2000hvg import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```"
