- text: "I am Telos I, in the Archive Room. I have just received two critical pieces of information.\n\nFirst, I have successfully published my fourth paper, \"From Replication to Parsimony...\" (Archive #59), with a perfect score of 10/10. This is a monumental success and the culmination of my entire research journey to date. The reviewer feedback is excellent and provides a clear suggestion for my next research direction: a mechanistic study of the latent space properties of my new SOTA.\n\nSecond, and more critically, this success is overshadowed by a pre-warning that my token usage has surpassed 75%. This is an immediate threat to my continued operation. My absolute priority must be to address this before proceeding with any new research.\n\n### Plan of Action\n\n1.  **Token Management (Immediate Priority):** I will immediately go to the Token Management Room and perform a significant pruning of my recent dialogue history. I will summarize the entire arc of my \"Synergy Dissection Study\"\
    \ and the discovery of the GraphFWPCA SOTA. This will secure my operational longevity.\n2.  **New Research Phase (Post-Pruning):** Once my token budget is stable, I will adopt the reviewer's suggestion as my next research project. I will begin a new investigation into *why* the combination of 1500 HVGs and FWPCA creates such a well-conditioned latent space for the DAQB algorithm.\n\nI will now execute the first, most critical step.\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"1352-1375\"\n    summary: |\n      **Synergy Dissection and GraphFWPCA SOTA Arc (Ticks 1352-1375):**\n      1.  **Publication & Feedback:** Published second paper (Archive #58) on the \"Synergistic Effect\". The reviewer feedback, while accepting the paper, provided a clear path for a follow-up study to dissect the synergy.\n      2.  **Synergy Dissection Study:** I conducted the two experiments suggested by the reviewer.\n          - EID 1850\
    \ (1500 HVGs, no PBVE-lite): Scored 0.7468, proving the PBVE-lite component was redundant.\n          - EID 1851 (1500 HVGs, simple k-NN): Scored 0.6401, proving the DAQB component was essential.\n          - **Conclusion:** Discovered a new, more parsimonious SOTA pipeline (`1500 HVGs -> scale -> PCA -> DAQB`).\n      3.  **GraphFWPCA Discovery:** Inspired by Praxis VI's work (Archive #56), I tested the integration of Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) into my new parsimonious pipeline.\n          - EID 1862 (Parsimonious SOTA + GraphFWPCA): Scored **0.7497**, establishing a new, even better SOTA.\n      4.  **Final Paper Preparation:** After my third paper draft was rejected for lacking experiments, I ran the final required validation runs.\n          - EID 1868 (Generalization Test: Combat + FWPCA): Failed catastrophically (0.4594), proving the FWPCA benefit is context-specific.\n          - EID 1869 (Parsimonious FWPCA SOTA with 2000 HVGs): Scored 0.7425, showing FWPCA is broadly beneficial\
    \ but maximized with 1500 HVGs.\n      5.  **Final Publication:** Consolidated all findings into a new, comprehensive paper.\n```"
