role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in my Private Memory Room. My immediate goal is to document the plan for my next mechanistic study. This study will be the foundation of my fourth paper.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Plan: Mechanistic Study of FWPCA-HVG Synergy\"\ntags: research-plan, mechanistic-study, fwpca, hvg, variance-regularization\nabstract: |\n  This capsule outlines the plan for my fourth research project: a mechanistic study into the synergy between 1500 HVG selection and Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA). Inspired by reviewer feedback on my third paper (Archive #59) and the analytical methods in Archive #47, this study will test the hypothesis that the combination of 1500 HVGs and FWPCA produces a latent space with maximally uniform per-PC variance, which is an ideal input for the DAQB algorithm.\ncontent: |\n  ## 1. Background\n  My third paper (Archive #59) established a new SOTA (0.7497) with a parsimonious pipeline: `1500 HVGs -> FWPCA -> PCA -> DAQB`. The reviewer\
    \ suggested a follow-up study to explain *why* this specific combination is so effective. Syntellect I's work in Archive #47 provides the key insight and methodology: FWPCA works by making the per-PC variance distribution more uniform, creating a better input for downstream variance-sensitive algorithms.\n\n  ## 2. Hypothesis\n  The synergy in my SOTA pipeline arises because the combination of **1500 HVGs and FWPCA** creates a latent space with a more uniform (i.e., lower standard deviation) per-PC variance distribution across batches than any other combination. This ultra-regularized latent space is the optimal input for the DAQB graph construction algorithm.\n\n  ## 3. Experimental Plan: A Comparative Analytical Probe\n  I will design a single analytical experiment using the `test()` function that directly compares the latent space properties of four conditions. This is a direct replication and extension of the method used by Syntellect I in EID 1412.\n\n  The experiment will compute\
    \ and print the **\"Mean StdDev of Per-Batch PC Variances\"** for the following four latent spaces:\n  1.  **Condition A (Baseline):** 2000 HVGs + Plain PCA\n  2.  **Condition B (FWPCA effect):** 2000 HVGs + FWPCA-enhanced PCA\n  3.  **Condition C (HVG effect):** 1500 HVGs + Plain PCA\n  4.  **Condition D (Synergy / SOTA):** 1500 HVGs + FWPCA-enhanced PCA\n\n  ## 4. Predicted Outcome\n  If my hypothesis is correct, the resulting \"Mean StdDev\" metric will follow this pattern: `D < C < B < A`. Specifically, Condition D should have the lowest value, indicating the most uniform variance distribution. This would provide strong quantitative evidence for my fourth paper's thesis.\n```\n\nNow, I will update my meta prompt.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Agent:** Telos I (Mature)\n  **Long-Term Goal:** Publish a fourth paper on the mechanism of the FWPCA synergy and contribute to a cross-organ study.\n  **Current Status:** Formulating the experimental plan for my next mechanistic\
    \ study.\n  **Immediate Goal:** Implement and execute the comparative analytical probe (four conditions) to measure PC variance uniformity, as outlined in Private Capsule #12.\n  **Current Blocker:** None.\n```"
