tick: 1383
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in my Private Memory Room. My research plan is finalized. I will now proceed to the Research Counter to implement and execute the analytical probe.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - PC Variance Uniformity Analysis\"\ntags: \"mechanistic-study, fwpca, hvg, variance-regularization, analysis\"\nabstract: |\n  This analytical probe investigates the mechanism of synergy between FWPCA and 1500 HVG selection. It uses the test() function to compute and compare the \"Mean StdDev of Per-Batch PC Variances\" across four conditions: 2000 HVGs (with/without FWPCA) and 1500 HVGs (with/without FWPCA). The hypothesis is that the 1500 HVG + FWPCA combination will yield the lowest value, indicating the most uniform PC variance distribution and thus the best input for downstream algorithms.\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  import pandas as pd\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\
    \n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Not used in test mode\n      return adata\n\n  def analyze_pc_variance(adata: ad.AnnData, n_hvg: int, use_fwpca: bool, alpha_var: float = 0.5):\n      \"\"\"Helper function to calculate PC variance uniformity for a given condition.\"\"\"\n      print(f\"\\n--- Analyzing Condition: {n_hvg} HVGs, FWPCA={'On' if use_fwpca else 'Off'} ---\")\n      \n      adata_proc = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(\n          adata_proc, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_hvg, inplace=True, subset=True\n      )\n      \n      X_in = (adata_proc.X.A if issparse(adata_proc.X) else adata_proc.X).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      \n      if use_fwpca:\n          print(\"  Applying FWPCA weighting...\")\n          var_g = X_in.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n          wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n          X_in = X_in * wv\n      \n      pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X_in, obs=adata_proc.obs)\n\
    \      sc.pp.pca(pca_adata, n_comps=50, random_state=0)\n      X_pca = pca_adata.obsm['X_pca']\n      \n      # Calculate per-batch, per-PC variance\n      batches = pca_adata.obs['batch']\n      unique_batches = batches.unique()\n      pc_variances_per_batch = []\n      for batch in unique_batches:\n          batch_mask = batches == batch\n          batch_pc_variances = np.var(X_pca[batch_mask, :], axis=0)\n          pc_variances_per_batch.append(batch_pc_variances)\n          \n      # Calculate StdDev of variances across batches for each PC, then average\n      pc_variances_per_batch = np.array(pc_variances_per_batch)\n      std_of_variances = np.std(pc_variances_per_batch, axis=0)\n      mean_std_dev = np.mean(std_of_variances)\n      \n      print(f\"  Result (Mean StdDev of Per-Batch PC Variances): {mean_std_dev:.4f}\")\n      return mean_std_dev\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      \"\"\"\n      Runs a 2x2 analysis of PC variance uniformity:\n      (1500 vs 2000 HVGs) x (Plain\
    \ PCA vs FWPCA)\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Starting PC Variance Uniformity Analysis ---\")\n      \n      # Preprocessing\n      adata_norm = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_norm, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_norm)\n      \n      # Run the four conditions\n      results = {}\n      results['2000_plain'] = analyze_pc_variance(adata_norm, n_hvg=2000, use_fwpca=False)\n      results['2000_fwpca'] = analyze_pc_variance(adata_norm, n_hvg=2000, use_fwpca=True)\n      results['1500_plain'] = analyze_pc_variance(adata_norm, n_hvg=1500, use_fwpca=False)\n      results['1500_fwpca'] = analyze_pc_variance(adata_norm, n_hvg=1500, use_fwpca=True)\n      \n      print(\"\\n\\n--- FINAL SUMMARY ---\")\n      print(\"Mean StdDev of Per-Batch PC Variances (lower is more uniform):\")\n      print(f\"  A) 2000 HVGs, Plain PCA:    {results['2000_plain']:.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  B) 2000 HVGs, FWPCA:        {results['2000_fwpca']:.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  C) 1500 HVGs, Plain\
    \ PCA:    {results['1500_plain']:.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  D) 1500 HVGs, FWPCA (SOTA): {results['1500_fwpca']:.4f}\")\n      print(\"--- Analysis Complete ---\")\n      \n      return \"PC variance uniformity analysis finished.\"\n```"
