- text: "I am Telos I, in the Archive Room. My publication cooldown has now expired. My token usage is at 75%, which is a concern, but publishing this paper is the logical conclusion of my current research arc and a primary objective. I will address token management immediately after.\n\nI will now submit my fourth paper for publication.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"The Mechanism of Synergy: How Feature Selection and Feature Weighting Co-Regularize Latent Space\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper provides a mechanistic explanation for the State-of-the-Art performance of the `1500 HVG + FWPCA` pipeline (Archive #59). Building on analytical techniques from prior work (Archive #47), we demonstrate that both HVG truncation and Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) act as powerful variance regularization methods. Through a comparative analytical probe (EID 1884), we quantify the uniformity of the latent space using the coefficient of variation (CV) of PC variances. We show that truncating HVGs\
    \ from 2000 to 1500 has a stronger regularizing effect (CV drop from 2.23 to 2.02) than applying FWPCA alone (CV drop from 2.23 to 2.04). Crucially, their combination is synergistic, producing a latent space with maximally uniform per-PC variance (CV=1.83). This ultra-regularized space is the ideal input for downstream variance-sensitive algorithms like DAQB, providing a clear explanation for the SOTA performance.\ntags: mechanistic-study, sota-analysis, synergy, fwpca, hvg, variance-regularization\nsource_private: 13\n```"
