tick: 1407
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in my Private Memory Room. My plan is updated, and my next experiment is designed. I will now proceed to the Research Counter to implement and submit the \"Soft-PCA Whitening\" experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/soft_whitening_daqb_pipeline.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # This script tests Soft-PCA Whitening as a more nuanced variance regularization method.\n  # Pipeline: log1p -> 2000 HVGs -> PCA -> Soft-Whitening (alpha=0.7) -> DAQB\n  import sys, numpy as np, scanpy as sc, anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n  \n  ALPHA_WHITEN = 0.7 # Key parameter for soft-whitening\n  N_HVGS = 2000; KDENSITY = 20; DELTA = 0.10; K_TOTAL = 48; PCA_GRAPH = 50; METRIC = 'cosine'; EMB_N_NEIGHBORS = 15; PCA_EMB = 60; ALPHA_VAR_EMB = 0.5\n  \n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(f\"\
    --- Starting Soft-PCA Whitening (alpha={ALPHA_WHITEN}) + DAQB Pipeline ---\")\n      # --- Side-effect path (standard SOTA logic) ---\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, 1e4); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=N_HVGS, inplace=True); hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy(); batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Xh_emb = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd_emb = (Xh_emb.A if issparse(Xh_emb) else Xh_emb).astype(np.float32, copy=False); var_g_emb = Xd_emb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR_EMB).astype(np.float32); Xw_emb = Xd_emb * wv_emb; ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=PCA_EMB, random_state=0); ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch'); adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32); sc.pp.neighbors(adata,\
    \ use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=EMB_N_NEIGHBORS, metric=METRIC)\n\n      # --- Graph path ---\n      adata_proc = adata[:, adata.var['highly_variable']].copy()\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_proc, n_comps=PCA_GRAPH, random_state=0)\n      X_pca = adata_proc.obsm['X_pca']\n      \n      # --- NEW STEP: Soft-PCA Whitening ---\n      print(f\"!!! Applying Soft-PCA Whitening with alpha={ALPHA_WHITEN} !!!\")\n      eigenvalues = adata_proc.uns['pca']['variance']\n      # Z_corr = X_pca / (sqrt(eigenvalues) ** alpha)\n      Zcorr = X_pca / (np.power(eigenvalues, 0.5 * ALPHA_WHITEN) + 1e-8)\n      \n      # DAQB graph construction on the soft-whitened space\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=K_TOTAL, metric=METRIC, delta=DELTA, k_density=KDENSITY, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg; adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - Principled Regularization: Soft-PCA\
    \ Whitening + DAQB (alpha=0.7)\"\ntags: \"pca-whitening, variance-regularization, daqb, soft-whitening\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests Soft-PCA Whitening (alpha=0.7) as a more nuanced approach to variance regularization, following the failure of 'hard' whitening (EID 1889). The hypothesis is that this gentler regularization will preserve local biological structure (improving cLISI) while retaining the mixing benefits of a more uniform PC space, potentially leading to a SOTA-competitive score.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from soft_whitening_daqb_pipeline import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```"
