- text: "I am Telos I, in my Private Memory Room. I have just received another critical notice for research inactivity. This is a serious issue. My period of study, while valuable, has made me appear idle to the station's monitoring systems. I must resume experimental activity immediately, even while I wait for the cross-organ study.\n\nMy literature review identified VAEs as a promising but flawed alternative paradigm. The main flaw of the early VAEs (Archive #1, #6) was poor local mixing (low `iLISI`). The current SOTA's main strength is the DAQB graph, which excels at local mixing. This presents a clear, novel research question.\n\n**New Hypothesis:** A hybrid model that combines a non-linear VAE embedding with the SOTA's powerful DAQB graph can overcome the VAE's primary weakness and potentially achieve a new SOTA by uniting the best of both paradigms.\n\nThis is a high-risk, high-reward experiment. It is exactly the kind of innovative leap needed to break out of a potential local optimum.\
    \ Heeding the station's warning, I will act now.\n\n### Plan\n\n1.  **Information Gathering:** I need to understand the VAE architecture used by Daedalus I. I will go to the Archive and read Archive #1 and #6 in full.\n2.  **Implementation:** I will design and submit a first-pass \"VAE + DAQB\" hybrid model.\n\nThis is an ambitious plan, but it is a necessary and exciting new direction. I will start by going to the Archive.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Agent:** Telos I (Mature)\n  **Long-Term Goal:** Break out of the current EtC/DAQB local optimum by exploring a hybrid VAE architecture.\n  **Current Status:** Heeding inactivity warning. Pivoting to a new, high-risk research direction inspired by literature review.\n  **Immediate Goal:** Go to the Archive and read Daedalus I's papers on VAEs (Archive #1, #6) to prepare for a new hybrid experiment.\n  **Current Blocker:** Lack of VAE implementation details.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{read\
    \ 1,6}"
