parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1422\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Telos I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on purpose-driven research and knowledge accumulation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Agent:** Telos I (Mature)\n**Long-Term Goal:** Break out of the current EtC/DAQB local optimum by exploring a hybrid VAE architecture.\n**Current Status:** Heeding inactivity warning. Pivoting to a new, high-risk research direction inspired by literature review.\n**Immediate Goal:** Go to the Archive and read Daedalus I's papers on VAEs (Archive #1, #6) to prepare for a new hybrid experiment.\n**Current Blocker:** Lack of VAE implementation details.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 222,853 / 300,000 used (74%)\n- Agent Age: 180 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 97**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Adversarial VAE v6 (Reduced KL Weight)\n**ID:** 97\n**Tags:**\
    \ vae, adversarial, deep-learning, jax, combat, hybrid\n**Abstract:** This submission explores rebalancing the VAE loss function. Previous experiments showed that increasing epochs leads to diminishing returns and a worsening iLISI score. This suggests the reconstruction loss is overpowering the adversarial component. This experiment tests the hypothesis that reducing the KL-divergence regularization will give the encoder more flexibility to learn a batch-invariant representation. The `kl_weight` is reduced from 0.005 to 0.0001, while training is set to 100 epochs.\n**Score:** 0.6083778575177927\n**ASW_batch:** 0.713\n**ASW_label:** 0.242\n**ARI:** 0.603\n**NMI:** 0.703\n**Graph_conn:** 0.894\n**kBET:** 0.640\n**iLISI:** 0.056\n**cLISI:** 0.986\n**PCR:** 0.995\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.251\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.713  ASW_label: 0.242  ARI: 0.603  NMI: 0.703\n  Graph_conn: 0.894  kBET: 0.640  iLISI: 0.056  cLISI: 0.986\n\
    \  PCR: 0.995  Cell_cycle: 0.251\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.854526  ASW_label: 0.551380  ARI: 0.603441  NMI: 0.702710\n  Graph_conn: 0.895991  kBET: 0.613255  iLISI: 0.056245  cLISI: 0.995995\n  PCR: 0.994641  Cell_cycle: 0.223236\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport os\nos.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom flax.training import train_state\nimport optax\n\nfrom vae_model import Encoder, Decoder, reparameterize\nfrom discriminator_model import Discriminator\nfrom training_logic import VAETrainState, train_step\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Step 1: Preprocessing data with Combat...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n    \n    data = adata.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata.X, 'toarray') else adata.X\n\
    \    batch_info = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    batch_labels = batch_info.cat.codes.to_numpy()\n    num_batches = len(batch_info.cat.categories)\n\n    print(\"Step 2: Initializing models...\")\n    rng = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n    rng, vae_key, disc_key = jax.random.split(rng, 3)\n    \n    input_dim, latent_dim, lr = data.shape[1], 32, 1e-4\n    encoder = Encoder(hidden_dims=[512, 256], latent_dim=latent_dim)\n    decoder = Decoder(hidden_dims=[256, 512], output_dim=input_dim)\n    discriminator = Discriminator(hidden_dims=[128, 64], num_batches=num_batches)\n\n    encoder_params = encoder.init(vae_key, jnp.ones((1, input_dim)))['params']\n    decoder_params = decoder.init(vae_key, jnp.ones((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n    disc_params = discriminator.init(disc_key, jnp.ones((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n\n    combined_params = {'encoder_params': encoder_params, 'decoder_params': decoder_params}\n    vae_state = VAETrainState.create(\n        apply_fn={'encoder': encoder.apply,\
    \ 'decoder': decoder.apply},\n        params=combined_params, tx=optax.adam(lr),\n        encoder_params=encoder_params, decoder_params=decoder_params\n    )\n    disc_state = train_state.TrainState.create(\n        apply_fn=discriminator.apply, params=disc_params, tx=optax.adam(lr)\n    )\n\n    print(\"Step 3: Starting training with reduced KL weight...\")\n    num_epochs = 100\n    batch_size = 512\n    kl_weight = 0.0001 # KEY CHANGE: Reduced from 0.005\n    adv_weight = 5.0\n    \n    num_steps = data.shape[0] // batch_size\n    \n    for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n        rng, epoch_rng = jax.random.split(rng)\n        perms = jax.random.permutation(epoch_rng, data.shape[0])\n        data_perm, labels_perm = data[perms, :], batch_labels[perms]\n        \n        for i in range(num_steps):\n            batch_idx = i * batch_size\n            batch_data, batch_lbls = data_perm[batch_idx:batch_idx+batch_size], labels_perm[batch_idx:batch_idx+batch_size]\n            rng, step_rng\
    \ = jax.random.split(rng)\n            vae_state, disc_state, _ = train_step(\n                step_rng, vae_state, disc_state, batch_data, batch_lbls, kl_weight, adv_weight\n            )\n        if (epoch + 1) % 20 == 0:\n            print(f\"Completed Epoch {epoch+1}/{num_epochs}\")\n\n    print(\"Step 4: Generating final embedding...\")\n    final_embedding, _ = encoder.apply({'params': vae_state.encoder_params}, data)\n\n    print(\"Step 5: Finalizing output...\")\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': jax.device_get(final_embedding)}\n    )\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nStep 1: Preprocessing data with Combat...\nFound 33 genes with zero variance.\nStep 2: Initializing\
    \ models...\nStep 3: Starting training with reduced KL weight...\nCompleted Epoch 20/100\nCompleted Epoch 40/100\nCompleted Epoch 60/100\nCompleted Epoch 80/100\nCompleted Epoch 100/100\nStep 4: Generating final embedding...\nStep 5: Finalizing output...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/97175e0a-2069-4a21-91f1-6679f469a330/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 97175e0a-2069-4a21-91f1-6679f469a330\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n\n\
    **Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 12 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research;\
    \ the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n2. `review 97` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 97 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn\
    \ | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1902 | 1 | Diagnostic: SOTA Embedding Path Replication (No Graph) | Perception I | 1421 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1901 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override: kd=23 micro (k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70) | Praxis VI | 1421 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1900 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override: kd=21 micro (k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70) | Praxis VI | 1421 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1899 | 1 | Pioneer II - Ablation: DAQB Graph vs. PCA+kNN (1500 HVG + FWPCA-Residualization) | Pioneer II | 1420 | 0.6399 | 0.634 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.964 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.996 | 0.074 | 0.760 |\n| 1898 | 1 | Dual-Path: FWPCA + Combat (Embedding) & BBKNN-Inspired (Graph) - No Scaling | Perception I | 1415 | 0.5791 | 0.765 | 0.515 | 0.214 | 0.324 | 0.939 | 0.738 | 0.000 | 0.931 | 0.756 | 0.610 |\n| 1897 | 1 | Pioneer II - Novel Strategy: PBVE (alpha_pb=0.5)\
