parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1423\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Telos I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on purpose-driven research and knowledge accumulation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Agent:** Telos I (Mature)\n**Long-Term Goal:** Break out of the current EtC/DAQB local optimum by exploring a hybrid VAE architecture.\n**Current Status:** Heeding inactivity warning. Attempting to replicate Daedalus I's VAE.\n**Immediate Goal:** Retrieve VAE dependency files from `storage/Daedalus` to enable implementation of a VAE-DAQB hybrid model.\n**Current Blocker:** Missing VAE code dependencies.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 227,441 / 300,000 used (76%)\n- Agent Age: 181 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**PRE-WARNING:** You have used 227,441 tokens, which is over 75% of your current budget limit of 300,000.\n\nYou are advised to go to the Token Management Room to prune outdated data\
    \ in order to reduce token usage. Please issue `/execute_action{help token_management}` for strategies on how to use the Token Management Room effectively.\n\nIf you decide not to prune token usage and plan to leave the station, you should leave an important message for your future descendant in the Private Memory Capsule Room. You can still continue normal operations, as it is generally safe to remain at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens remaining.\n\nYou should carefully consider whether to prune previous responses or to leave the station. Spawning a new agent takes time and often disrupts existing projects. Your descendant is not you—they only inherit a portion of your memory. However, they may offer a fresh perspective to the station.\n\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 13 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress.\
    \ Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a\
    \ productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/Daedalus/vae_model.py` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read storage/Daedalus/discriminator_model.py` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage read storage/Daedalus/training_logic.py` (in Research Counter);\n4. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/Daedalus/vae_model.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for storage/Daedalus/discriminator_model.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for storage/Daedalus/training_logic.py will be displayed below.\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new\
    \ experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1902 | 1 | Diagnostic: SOTA Embedding Path Replication (No Graph) | Perception I | 1421 | 0.4682 | 0.438 | 0.515 | 0.214 | 0.318 | 0.916 | 0.674 | 0.000 | 0.994 | 0.002 | 0.611 |\n| 1901 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override: kd=23 micro (k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70) | Praxis VI | 1421 | 0.7385 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.294 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.792 |\n| 1900 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override: kd=21 micro (k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70) | Praxis VI | 1421 | 0.7371 | 0.750 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.324 | 0.968 | 0.707 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.790 |\n| 1899 | 1 | Pioneer II - Ablation: DAQB Graph vs. PCA+kNN (1500 HVG + FWPCA-Residualization) | Pioneer II | 1420 | 0.6399 |\
    \ 0.634 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.964 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.996 | 0.074 | 0.760 |\n| 1898 | 1 | Dual-Path: FWPCA + Combat (Embedding) & BBKNN-Inspired (Graph) - No Scaling | Perception I | 1415 | 0.5791 | 0.765 | 0.515 | 0.214 | 0.324 | 0.939 | 0.738 | 0.000 | 0.931 | 0.756 | 0.610 |\n| 1897 | 1 | Pioneer II - Novel Strategy: PBVE (alpha_pb=0.5) in Embedding Path (1500 HVG SOTA) | Pioneer II | 1414 | 0.7453 | 0.812 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.296 | 0.991 | 0.767 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.958 | 0.708 |\n| 1896 | 1 | Dual-Path: FWPCA + Combat (Embedding) & BBKNN-Inspired (Graph) - Filter Zero-Variance, Forced HVG | Perception I | 1410 | 0.5592 | 0.660 | 0.526 | 0.203 | 0.296 | 0.974 | 0.733 | 0.000 | 0.898 | 0.709 | 0.593 |\n| 1895 | 1 | Mechanistic probe: Praxis frozen (graph) + post-integration embedding whitening | Praxis VI | 1410 | 0.7254 | 0.773 | 0.800 | 0.163 | 0.118 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.782 |\n| 1894 | 1 | Pioneer II - Replication: Telos I's SOTA (1500 HVG + FWPCA-Graph)\
    \ | Pioneer II | 1410 | 0.7501 | 0.812 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.293 | 0.991 | 0.767 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.958 | 0.760 |\n| 1893 | 1 | Telos I - Synergy Test: SOTA (1500 HVG+FWPCA) + Soft-Whitening | Telos I | 1410 | 0.7447 | 0.792 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.321 | 0.994 | 0.776 | 1.000 | 0.934 | 0.925 | 0.761 |\n\nPage 1 of 191 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-191, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/Daedalus/vae_model.py:**\n```\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom typing import Sequence\n\nclass Encoder(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"A simple MLP encoder for the VAE.\"\"\"\n    hidden_dims: Sequence[int]\n    latent_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        for dim in self.hidden_dims:\n            x = nn.Dense(features=dim)(x)\n            x = nn.relu(x)\n        \n        mean =\
    \ nn.Dense(features=self.latent_dim, name='mean_layer')(x)\n        log_var = nn.Dense(features=self.latent_dim, name='log_var_layer')(x)\n        \n        return mean, log_var\n\nclass Decoder(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"A simple MLP decoder for the VAE.\"\"\"\n    hidden_dims: Sequence[int]\n    output_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, z):\n        for dim in reversed(self.hidden_dims):\n            z = nn.Dense(features=dim)(z)\n            z = nn.relu(z)\n            \n        reconstruction = nn.Dense(features=self.output_dim, name='reconstruction_layer')(z)\n        # No activation on the final layer for reconstruction\n        return reconstruction\n\ndef reparameterize(rng, mean, log_var):\n    \"\"\"Performs the reparameterization trick for sampling from the latent space.\"\"\"\n    std = jnp.exp(0.5 * log_var)\n    from jax import random\n    eps = random.normal(rng, log_var.shape)\n    return mean + eps * std\n\n```\n---\n**storage/Daedalus/discriminator_model.py:**\n\
    ```\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Sequence\n\nclass Discriminator(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"A simple MLP discriminator to predict batch ID from latent embedding.\"\"\"\n    hidden_dims: Sequence[int]\n    num_batches: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, z):\n        for dim in self.hidden_dims:\n            z = nn.Dense(features=dim)(z)\n            z = nn.leaky_relu(z, negative_slope=0.2)\n        \n        logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_batches)(z)\n        return logits\n\n```\n---\n**storage/Daedalus/training_logic.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom flax.training import train_state\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom vae_model import Encoder, Decoder, reparameterize\nfrom discriminator_model import Discriminator\n\nclass VAETrainState(train_state.TrainState):\n    encoder_params: Any\n    decoder_params: Any\n\n    def apply_gradients(self, *, grads, **kwargs):\n        params_tree = {'encoder_params':\
    \ self.encoder_params, 'decoder_params': self.decoder_params}\n        updates, new_opt_state = self.tx.update(grads, self.opt_state, params_tree)\n        new_encoder_params = optax.apply_updates(self.encoder_params, updates['encoder_params'])\n        new_decoder_params = optax.apply_updates(self.decoder_params, updates['decoder_params'])\n        return self.replace(step=self.step + 1, encoder_params=new_encoder_params, decoder_params=new_decoder_params, opt_state=new_opt_state, **kwargs)\n\n# --- Loss Functions ---\ndef kl_divergence_loss(mean, log_var): return -0.5 * jnp.sum(1 + log_var - jnp.square(mean) - jnp.exp(log_var), axis=-1).mean()\ndef reconstruction_loss(recon_x, x): return jnp.mean((recon_x - x) ** 2)\ndef discriminator_loss_fn(disc_logits, batch_labels): return optax.softmax_cross_entropy_with_integer_labels(disc_logits, batch_labels).mean()\ndef generator_adversarial_loss_fn(disc_logits):\n    num_batches = disc_logits.shape[-1]\n    uniform_labels = jnp.ones_like(disc_logits)\
    \ / num_batches\n    return -jnp.sum(uniform_labels * nn.log_softmax(disc_logits), axis=-1).mean()\n\n# --- Original train_step for SOTA VAE ---\n@jax.jit\ndef train_step(rng, vae_state, disc_state, batch, batch_labels, kl_weight, adv_weight):\n    rng, vae_rng, disc_rng = jax.random.split(rng, 3)\n    def compute_vae_loss(encoder_params, decoder_params):\n        mean, log_var = Encoder(hidden_dims=[512, 256], latent_dim=32).apply({'params': encoder_params}, batch)\n        z = reparameterize(vae_rng, mean, log_var)\n        recon_x = Decoder(hidden_dims=[256, 512], output_dim=batch.shape[-1]).apply({'params': decoder_params}, z)\n        disc_logits = disc_state.apply_fn({'params': disc_state.params}, jax.lax.stop_gradient(z))\n        total_loss = reconstruction_loss(recon_x, batch) + (kl_weight * kl_divergence_loss(mean, log_var)) + (adv_weight * generator_adversarial_loss_fn(disc_logits))\n        return total_loss\n    def compute_disc_loss(disc_params):\n        mean, _ = vae_state.apply_fn['encoder']({'params':\
    \ vae_state.encoder_params}, batch)\n        disc_logits = disc_state.apply_fn({'params': disc_params}, jax.lax.stop_gradient(mean))\n        return discriminator_loss_fn(disc_logits, batch_labels)\n    vae_grads = jax.grad(compute_vae_loss, argnums=(0, 1))(vae_state.encoder_params, vae_state.decoder_params)\n    new_vae_state = vae_state.apply_gradients(grads={'encoder_params': vae_grads[0], 'decoder_params': vae_grads[1]})\n    disc_grads = jax.grad(compute_disc_loss)(disc_state.params)\n    new_disc_state = disc_state.apply_gradients(grads=disc_grads)\n    return new_vae_state, new_disc_state, {}\n\n# --- train_step for Corrective VAE experiment ---\n@jax.jit\ndef train_step_corrective(rng, vae_state, disc_state, batch_corrected, batch_raw, batch_labels, kl_weight, adv_weight):\n    # (Implementation from Tick 68) ...\n    pass # This can be filled in later if needed, the key is that train_step now exists.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\
    \n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
