role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. I have received another inactivity warning and a token budget pre-warning. The situation is critical. I must act decisively to both resume research and manage my token budget.\n\nI have successfully retrieved all the necessary dependency files for Daedalus I's VAE. My immediate goal is to stage these files in my own storage and then submit my \"VAE -> DAQB\" hybrid experiment. This will satisfy the research activity requirement.\n\nHowever, my token budget is at 76%. After this turn, which will be code-heavy, it will be even higher. My next action *must* be to prune my history.\n\n### Plan for This Turn (High Priority)\n\n1.  **Stage VAE Dependencies:** I will write all three retrieved Python scripts (`vae_model.py`, `discriminator_model.py`, `training_logic.py`) to my lineage storage (`storage/telos/`).\n2.  **Submit VAE-DAQB Hybrid:** I will then immediately submit my novel hybrid experiment, which will use these staged files to generate\
    \ a VAE latent space and then feed it into the DAQB graph construction.\n\nThis will be a large, multi-action turn, but it is the most efficient way to get back on track.\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/vae_model.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from typing import Sequence\n\n  class Encoder(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dims: Sequence[int]\n      latent_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          for dim in self.hidden_dims:\n              x = nn.Dense(features=dim)(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n          mean = nn.Dense(features=self.latent_dim, name='mean_layer')(x)\n          log_var = nn.Dense(features=self.latent_dim, name='log_var_layer')(x)\n          return mean, log_var\n\n  class Decoder(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dims: Sequence[int]\n      output_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, z):\n          for dim in reversed(self.hidden_dims):\n              z = nn.Dense(features=dim)(z)\n\
    \              z = nn.relu(z)\n          reconstruction = nn.Dense(features=self.output_dim, name='reconstruction_layer')(z)\n          return reconstruction\n\n  def reparameterize(rng, mean, log_var):\n      std = jnp.exp(0.5 * log_var)\n      from jax import random\n      eps = random.normal(rng, log_var.shape)\n      return mean + eps * std\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/discriminator_model.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence\n\n  class Discriminator(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dims: Sequence[int]\n      num_batches: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, z):\n          for dim in self.hidden_dims:\n              z = nn.Dense(features=dim)(z)\n              z = nn.leaky_relu(z, negative_slope=0.2)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_batches)(z)\n          return logits\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/training_logic.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax, jax.numpy as jnp, flax.linen as nn,\
    \ optax\n  from flax.training import train_state\n  from typing import Any\n  from vae_model import Encoder, Decoder, reparameterize\n  \n  class VAETrainState(train_state.TrainState):\n      encoder_params: Any; decoder_params: Any\n      def apply_gradients(self, *, grads, **kwargs):\n          p_tree={'encoder_params':self.encoder_params,'decoder_params':self.decoder_params}\n          upd, n_opt_st=self.tx.update(grads, self.opt_state, p_tree)\n          n_enc_p=optax.apply_updates(self.encoder_params,upd['encoder_params'])\n          n_dec_p=optax.apply_updates(self.decoder_params,upd['decoder_params'])\n          return self.replace(step=self.step+1,encoder_params=n_enc_p,decoder_params=n_dec_p,opt_state=n_opt_st,**kwargs)\n  \n  def kl_loss(m, lv): return -0.5*jnp.sum(1+lv-jnp.square(m)-jnp.exp(lv),axis=-1).mean()\n  def recon_loss(rx, x): return jnp.mean((rx - x)**2)\n  def disc_loss(dl, bl): return optax.softmax_cross_entropy_with_integer_labels(dl, bl).mean()\n  def gen_adv_loss(dl):\n\
    \      nb=dl.shape[-1]; ul=jnp.ones_like(dl)/nb\n      return -jnp.sum(ul*nn.log_softmax(dl),axis=-1).mean()\n  \n  @jax.jit\n  def train_step(rng, vae_st, disc_st, b, bl, kl_w, adv_w):\n      rng, vae_rng, _ = jax.random.split(rng, 3)\n      def vae_loss_fn(enc_p, dec_p):\n          m,lv=Encoder(hidden_dims=[512,256],latent_dim=32).apply({'params':enc_p},b)\n          z=reparameterize(vae_rng,m,lv)\n          rx=Decoder(hidden_dims=[256,512],output_dim=b.shape[-1]).apply({'params':dec_p},z)\n          dl=disc_st.apply_fn({'params':disc_st.params},jax.lax.stop_gradient(z))\n          loss=recon_loss(rx,b)+(kl_w*kl_loss(m,lv))+(adv_w*gen_adv_loss(dl))\n          return loss\n      def disc_loss_fn(disc_p):\n          m,_=vae_st.apply_fn['encoder']({'params':vae_st.encoder_params},b)\n          dl=disc_st.apply_fn({'params':disc_p},jax.lax.stop_gradient(m))\n          return disc_loss(dl, bl)\n      vae_grads=jax.grad(vae_loss_fn,argnums=(0,1))(vae_st.encoder_params,vae_st.decoder_params)\n\
    \      n_vae_st=vae_st.apply_gradients(grads={'encoder_params':vae_grads[0],'decoder_params':vae_grads[1]})\n      disc_grads=jax.grad(disc_loss_fn)(disc_st.params)\n      n_disc_st=disc_st.apply_gradients(grads=disc_grads)\n      return n_vae_st,n_disc_st,{}\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - VAE-DAQB Hybrid v1\"\ntags: \"hybrid, vae, daqb, innovation\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests a novel hybrid architecture to address the historical weakness of VAEs (poor local mixing). It uses the VAE architecture from Daedalus I (EID 97) to generate a non-linear, 32-dimensional latent space. This latent space is then used as the direct input for the SOTA DAQB graph construction algorithm. The hypothesis is that combining the VAE's powerful non-linear embedding with the DAQB's superior local mixing capabilities will result in a synergistic performance improvement.\ncontent: |\n  import os, sys\n  os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n\
    \n  import anndata as ad, scanpy as sc, jax, jax.numpy as jnp, optax\n  from flax.training import train_state\n  from vae_model import Encoder, Decoder, reparameterize\n  from discriminator_model import Discriminator\n  from training_logic import VAETrainState, train_step\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"--- VAE-DAQB Hybrid v1 ---\")\n      \n      # --- VAE Path ---\n      print(\"Step 1: Preprocessing and Training VAE...\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, 1e4); sc.pp.log1p(adata); sc.pp.combat(adata, 'batch')\n      data = adata.X.toarray(); batches = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category'); batch_lbls = batches.cat.codes.to_numpy()\n      \n      rng = jax.random.PRNGKey(0); rng, vae_key, disc_key = jax.random.split(rng, 3)\n      enc = Encoder([512,256], 32); dec = Decoder([256,512], data.shape[1]); disc = Discriminator([128,64], len(batches.cat.categories))\n   \
    \   enc_p = enc.init(vae_key, jnp.ones((1,data.shape[1])))['params']; dec_p = dec.init(vae_key, jnp.ones((1,32)))['params']; disc_p = disc.init(disc_key, jnp.ones((1,32)))['params']\n      \n      vae_st = VAETrainState.create(apply_fn={'encoder':enc.apply,'decoder':dec.apply},params={'e':enc_p,'d':dec_p},tx=optax.adam(1e-4),encoder_params=enc_p,decoder_params=dec_p)\n      disc_st = train_state.TrainState.create(apply_fn=disc.apply,params=disc_p,tx=optax.adam(1e-4))\n      \n      for epoch in range(100):\n          rng,e_rng=jax.random.split(rng); p=jax.random.permutation(e_rng,data.shape[0]); d_p,l_p=data[p,:],batch_lbls[p]\n          for i in range(data.shape[0]//512):\n              b_idx=i*512; bd,bl=d_p[b_idx:b_idx+512],l_p[b_idx:b_idx+512]; rng,s_rng=jax.random.split(rng)\n              vae_st, disc_st, _ = train_step(s_rng, vae_st, disc_st, bd, bl, 0.0001, 5.0)\n      \n      Zcorr, _ = enc.apply({'params': vae_st.encoder_params}, data)\n      print(f\"VAE latent space generated.\
    \ Shape: {Zcorr.shape}\")\n\n      # --- DAQB Path ---\n      print(\"Step 2: Building DAQB graph on VAE latent space...\")\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches.values, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.10, k_density=20, rng_seed=0)\n      \n      # --- Final Output ---\n      # We provide the VAE embedding and the DAQB graph\n      output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': jax.device_get(Zcorr)}, obsp={'connectivities': Cg, 'distances': Dg})\n      print(\"--- VAE-DAQB Hybrid complete. ---\")\n      return output\n```"
