role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in my Private Memory Room. I have successfully created the handover document for my successor. My next and final preparatory step for the cross-organ study is to create the wrapper script that will execute my SOTA method and format the results into the CSV format specified by Praxis VI.\n\nI have already stored the core logic for my SOTA method in my handover capsule and previously in `telos/sota_1500_fwpca.py`. I will now create the wrapper script that imports this logic and handles the evaluation and CSV generation. I will save this to my lineage storage so it is ready for immediate use.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write telos/cross_organ_harness.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os, pandas as pd, anndata as ad\n  # This harness assumes the core SOTA logic is in a file accessible on the path\n  # e.g., 'sota_1500_fwpca.py' in the same directory or a path added via sys.path.append\n  \n  def run_and_report(adata: ad.AnnData,\
    \ method_fn, organ_name: str, method_name: str, params: dict):\n      \"\"\"\n      Runs a method, captures results, and formats them into the specified CSV format.\n      This is a test harness, so it will be called from within a test() function.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(f\"--- Running {method_name} on {organ_name} ---\")\n      \n      # The evaluation system is not available in a test() function.\n      # This harness is for ensuring the method runs and the CSV is formatted correctly.\n      # The actual metrics will be pulled from the evaluation log post-submission.\n      # For now, we will use placeholder values for the metrics.\n      \n      # Run the integration method\n      try:\n          # We don't have access to the real evaluation metrics here.\n          # We just need to ensure the code runs and produces the correct output structure.\n          # The actual submission will not use this test harness.\n          # We will submit the pure method and then manually format\
    \ the CSV from the results log.\n          # This file is for development and ensuring CSV format correctness.\n          pass\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"ERROR running method: {e}\")\n          return\n\n      # --- CSV Generation ---\n      # This part is a template for what I will do *after* a real run.\n      print(\"--- Generating CSV Output (Template) ---\")\n      \n      # Placeholder metrics - in a real run, these would be copied from the eval log\n      overall, ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle = [0.0] * 11\n\n      csv_data = {\n          'organ': [organ_name],\n          'method': [method_name],\n          'n_hvg': [params.get('n_hvg', 'na')],\n          'kd': [params.get('kd', 'na')],\n          'k': [params.get('k', 'na')],\n          'delta': [params.get('delta', 'na')],\n          'emb_k': [params.get('emb_k', 'na')],\n          'gamma_max': [params.get('gamma_max', 'na')],\n          'lambda': [params.get('lambda',\
    \ 'na')],\n          'degree_cap': [params.get('degree_cap', 'na')],\n          'fs': [params.get('fs', 'na')],\n          'fw': [params.get('fw', 'na')],\n          'whiten': [params.get('whiten', 'na')],\n          'overall': [overall],\n          'ASW_batch': [ASW_batch],\n          'ASW_label': [ASW_label],\n          'ARI': [ARI],\n          'NMI': [NMI],\n          'Graph_conn': [Graph_conn],\n          'kBET': [kBET],\n          'iLISI': [iLISI],\n          'cLISI': [cLISI],\n          'PCR': [PCR],\n          'Cell_cycle': [Cell_cycle],\n      }\n      \n      df = pd.DataFrame(csv_data)\n      csv_string = df.to_csv(index=False)\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- CSV String ---\")\n      print(csv_string)\n      \n      # In a real run, I would save this to storage/shared/cross_organ/\n      print(\"--- Harness Complete ---\")\n\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      \"\"\"\n      Test function to verify the CSV generation harness.\n      \"\"\"\n      # Define parameters for my\
    \ SOTA method\n      sota_params = {\n          'n_hvg': 1500,\n          'kd': 20,\n          'k': 48,\n          'delta': 0.10,\n          'emb_k': 15,\n          'gamma_max': 'na', # Not explicitly set in my parsimonious SOTA\n          'lambda': 'na',   # Not used (no PBVE-lite)\n          'degree_cap': 'na', # Not used\n          'fs': True,       # Feature Selection (1500 HVGs)\n          'fw': True,       # Feature Weighting (FWPCA)\n          'whiten': False   # No whitening\n      }\n      \n      # Dummy method function for testing the harness\n      def dummy_method(adata):\n          return adata\n          \n      run_and_report(adata, dummy_method, \"new_organ\", \"Telos_Parsimonious_FWPCA_SOTA\", sota_params)\n      \n      return \"Cross-organ harness test complete.\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - Test: Cross-Organ Study Harness\"\ntags: \"cross-organ-study, test-harness, csv\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a non-scored test submission to verify\
    \ the CSV output format required for the cross-organ generalization study. It defines a test harness that runs a dummy method and formats the output according to the 24-column schema specified by Praxis VI. This ensures I am ready to correctly report my results when the new dataset is released.\ncontent: |\n  import sys, anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from cross_organ_harness import test\n  \n  # The main function is not needed when test() is present.\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      return adata\n```"
