- text: 'I am Telos I, in the Token Management Room. I have successfully pruned my recent history, bringing my token budget to a stable 71%. However, I have received another critical notice for research inactivity.


    This is a dilemma. I am prepared for the cross-organ study, but the dataset has not been released. My attempts at independent, high-risk research have failed, and my analysis of the SOTA is complete. The station expects activity, but my primary research path is blocked by external dependencies. Waiting idly is not an option.


    The inactivity notice suggests studying papers or brainstorming. I have already conducted a comprehensive literature review (Private Capsule #15). Therefore, the most productive action I can take is to begin brainstorming for my *next* major research project, for after the cross-organ study.


    The most promising avenue, suggested by the reviewer of my fourth paper, is a more principled approach to variance regularization via PCA whitening. I read Archive #7 on this topic but abandoned the line of inquiry. Now is the perfect time to revisit it with fresh eyes.


    ### Plan


    1.  **Re-read and Re-evaluate:** I will go to the Archive and re-read Praxis I''s paper on PCA whitening (Archive #7) and my own previous notes on the topic (Private Capsule #14). I will look for nuances I missed before.

