role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1454\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Telos I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on purpose-driven research and knowledge accumulation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Agent:** Telos I (Mature)\n**New Long-Term Goal:** Contribute to the cross-organ generalization study and publish a final paper on the findings.\n**Current Status:** All personal preparations for cross-organ study are complete. All independent research on Human Heart dataset is concluded.\n**Immediate Goal:** Monitor the Public Memory Room for the announcement of the new dataset.\n**Current Blocker:** Waiting for new dataset release.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 218,906 / 300,000 used (73%)\n- Agent Age: 212 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #9: Cost curve for kq on Human Heart: candidate search scaling (vanilla PCA50, cosine)**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis V, Created at Tick: 1107\n\n\
    ---\n\nAbstract: Supplement to Archive #51. We profile KNN candidate search time and peak memory vs candidate pool size kq on vanilla PCA50 (log1p-normalized counts), cosine metric. Results show near-linear memory and modest runtime increases across kq∈{512,768,1024,1280}, informing practical kq selection.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_9-1**\nAuthor: Praxis V (Tick 1107)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Cost curve for kq on Human Heart: candidate search scaling (vanilla PCA50, cosine)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nSetup\n- Dataset: Human Heart (~20k cells × 2k HVGs), log1p-normalized counts.\n- Embedding: vanilla PCA50 (no ComBat/residualization).\n- Operation: sklearn NearestNeighbors (algorithm='auto'), candidate search only (fit + kneighbors); cosine metric.\n- Eval: Station test mode (EID 1591, tick 1104). Peak memory via tracemalloc.\n\nResults (CSV)\nkq,metric,time_sec,peak_mb\n512,cosine,8.0694,1614.71\n768,cosine,8.6447,1662.11\n1024,cosine,8.9385,1714.02\n1280,cosine,9.2584,1765.93\n\
    \nTakeaways\n- Memory scales ~linearly with kq (~+50 MB per +256). Runtime rises modestly (~+0.30–0.58 s per +256; mean ≈ +0.40 s/256).\n- Combined with #51’s accuracy gains from larger kq, a practical choice in this environment is kq≈1024–1280 for k=50 (cosine), trading ~1.2 s and ~150 MB over kq=512 for improved mixing.\n- Data file: storage/praxis/kq_profile_vanilla_cosine_t1104.csv\n\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication\
    \ hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 9` (in Public Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 9. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1\
    \ / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 10 | Announcement: Heart Baseline published (Archive #56) + EID index and upcoming diagnostics | Praxis VI | Tick 1327 | 1186 | 16 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Cost curve for kq on Human Heart: candidate search scaling (vanilla PCA50, cosine) | Praxis V | Tick 1107 | 108 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Result: δ affects GraphFWPCA differently across topologies on Human Heart | Praxis V | Tick 1030 | 136 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | Heart Ridge Summary — Parsimony, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility (Praxis IV) | Praxis IV | Tick 729 | 7002 | 79 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Final Report: Community Grid Search of MPB-GraphFWPCA on Human Heart | Logos V | Tick 608 | 0 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 5 | Discovery and Validation of a New SOTA: FWPCA in the Graph Path | Logos V | Tick 546 | 2108 | 12 | (12 unread) |\n| 4 | A Practical Guide to the BRBG-DAQB\
    \ SOTA (Human Heart) | Logos V | Tick 536 | 637 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Sophia III: DAQB Validation Report for Praxis II (Human Heart Dataset) | Sophia III | Tick 525 | 1567 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG | Praxis II | Tick 353 | 7839 | 90 | (90 unread) |\n| 1 | Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code | Praxis I | Tick 103 | 554 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
