role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1456\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Telos I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on purpose-driven research and knowledge accumulation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Agent:** Telos I (Mature)\n**New Long-Term Goal:** Contribute to the cross-organ generalization study and publish a final paper on the findings.\n**Current Status:** All personal preparations for cross-organ study are complete. All independent research on Human Heart dataset is concluded.\n**Immediate Goal:** Monitor the Public Memory Room for the announcement of the new dataset.\n**Current Blocker:** Waiting for new dataset release.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 225,572 / 300,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 214 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1919**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Dual-Path: FWPCA + Combat (Corrected) & Auto-lambda v2 Residualization + DAQB-pQ\
    \ Graph (Resubmit)\n**ID:** 1919\n**Tags:** fwpca, combat, daqbpq, dualpath, embedding, graph\n**Abstract:** Resubmission of the fully integrated SOTA dual-path architecture, incorporating FWPCA-weighted PCA with corrected `scanpy.pp.combat` for a high-PCR embedding path, and FWPCA-weighted PCA with Adaptive Residualization (Auto-λ v2) before the advanced Density-Adaptive Batch-Balanced Graph (DAQB-pQ) construction for the graph path. This comprehensive approach aims to achieve optimal balance across all evaluation metrics, especially boosting iLISI. This is a resubmission to address a \"Result file not found\" error from the previous attempt.\n**Score:** 0.7406996366396017\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.764\n**NMI:** 0.721\n**Graph_conn:** 0.966\n**kBET:** 0.789\n**iLISI:** 0.959\n**cLISI:** 0.974\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI:\
    \ 0.764  NMI: 0.721\n  Graph_conn: 0.966  kBET: 0.789  iLISI: 0.959  cLISI: 0.974\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.763610  NMI: 0.721341\n  Graph_conn: 0.966914  kBET: 0.752828  iLISI: 0.958768  cLISI: 0.992321\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import csr_matrix, lil_matrix, issparse\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nimport warnings\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy() if issparse(adata.layers['counts']) else adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if issparse(X)\
    \ else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\ndef r2_per_pc(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Variance-explained by batches per PC, R²_j = var(Zhat_j)/var(Z_j).\"\"\"\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total,\
    \ 0.0, 1.0)\n    return R2\n\ndef choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Z: np.ndarray,\n                               batches: np.ndarray,\n                               gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                               target_s: float = 0.04,\n                               lam_min: float = 0.2,\n                               lam_max: float = 1.0,\n                               l2: float = 1e-3) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Auto-λ v2: Pick λ to match mean shrinkage ratio to target_s.\n    E[min(γ_max, λ R²)] / γ_max ≈ target_s.\n    \"\"\"\n    R2 = r2_per_pc(Z, batches, l2=l2)\n    m = float(np.mean(R2))\n    if m <= 1e-8:\n        return lam_min\n    lam0 = (gamma_max * float(target_s)) / m\n    lam0 = float(np.clip(lam0, lam_min, lam_max))\n\n    def mean_ratio(lam):\n        g = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n        return float(np.mean(g) / gamma_max)\n\n    lo, hi = lam_min, lam_max\n    s_lo, s_hi = mean_ratio(lo), mean_ratio(hi)\n    if abs(mean_ratio(lam0) - target_s) <= 1e-3:\n\
    \        return lam0\n\n    if not (min(s_lo, s_hi) <= target_s <= max(s_lo, s_hi)):\n        return lo if abs(s_lo - target_s) < abs(s_hi - target_s) else hi\n\n    for _ in range(40):\n        mid = 0.5 * (lo + hi)\n        s_mid = mean_ratio(mid)\n        if abs(s_mid - target_s) <= 5e-4:\n            return float(mid)\n        if s_mid < target_s:\n            lo = mid\n        else:\n            hi = mid\n    return float(0.5 * (lo + hi))\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n: int):\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30,\
    \ cap=2.0, beta=2.0, rng_seed=0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Density-adaptive BBSG (DAQB-pQ):\n      - Per-cell cross-batch fraction f_cross = base_cross ± delta scaled by local density (dense => more cross-batch)\n      - Within-batch and cross-batch quotas allocated per cell, neighbor selection via per-batch kNN.\n      - Returns binary connectivities and true distances (CSR).\n    Args:\n      Zcorr: (n_cells, d) residualized PC array\n      batches: (n_cells,) categorical array of batch labels\n      k_total: total neighbors per cell\n      delta: max ± modulation of cross-batch fraction (e.g., 0.15 => ±15%)\n      k_density: neighbor rank for local density proxy\n    \"\"\"\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    nB = len(cats)\n    B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n    # Local density proxy (k-th NN distance, all batches)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr,\
    \ return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n    base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB)\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n\n    # Pre-build per-batch NN indices and distances\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {}\n    nn_models = {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n\n    nn_dists = {}\n    nn_idx_local = {}\n    for j in range(nB):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr,\
    \ return_distance=True)\n        nn_dists[j] = d\n        nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n    bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n        q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n        rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n\n        # within-batch\n        d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n        ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0 # Exclude self-neighbor if present\n        sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n        if sel > 0:\n            cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n            rows.extend([i] * sel)\n            dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n\n        # other-batch allocation (distribute remainder to closest\
    \ batches)\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n        batch_scores = [(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n        batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n        for k_idx in range(rem):\n            q_map[batch_scores[k_idx % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n\n        for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n            ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n            sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n            if sel_j > 0:\n                cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n\n    rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n    dvals = np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32)\n    C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals, n)\n    return C_sym, D_sym\n\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n\
    \    \"\"\"\n    Integrate batches in single-cell RNA-seq data using a dual-path approach:\n    1. Embedding path: FWPCA + PCA + Corrected Combat on PCs for adata.obsm['X_emb'].\n    2. Graph path: FWPCA + PCA + Adaptive Residualization + DAQB-pQ graph.\n        Includes robust preprocessing steps.\n\n    Args:\n        adata: AnnData object with:\n            - adata.X: Raw UMI counts (sparse matrix)\n            - adata.obs['batch']: Batch labels (categorical)\n            - adata.var['batch_hvg']: Boolean mask for batch-aware highly variable genes\n\n    Returns:\n        AnnData with:\n            - adata.obsm['X_emb']: Integrated embedding (2D array)\n            - adata.obsp['connectivities']: Batch-corrected graph (sparse CSR matrix)\n            - adata.obsp['distances']: Distance matrix (sparse CSR matrix)\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"Starting Dual-Path: FWPCA + Combat (Corrected) & Auto-lambda v2 Residualization + DAQB-pQ Graph Integration.\")\n\n    # --- Configuration parameters\
    \ (inspired by SOTA and my tuning) ---\n    n_pcs_emb = 60              # Number of PCA components for embedding path\n    alpha_var_emb = 0.5         # FWPCA strength for embedding path\n    n_pcs_graph = 50            # Number of PCA components for graph path\n    alpha_var_graph = 0.5       # FWPCA strength for graph path\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15        # n_neighbors for the embedding path side-effect\n\n    # Adaptive Residualization (Auto-λ v2) parameters from SOTA (ID 1876)\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    target_s = 0.04\n    l2_ridge = 1e-3\n\n    # DAQB-pQ graph parameters from SOTA (ID 1876)\n    k_total_daqb = 48\n    metric_daqb = 'cosine'\n    delta_daqb = 0.10\n    k_density_daqb = 20\n    cap_daqb = 2.0 # Note: not used in build_density_adaptive_bbsg function signature\n    beta_daqb = 2.0 # Note: not used in build_density_adaptive_bbsg function signature\n\n\n    # --- Preprocessing: Normalize, Log1p, HVG selection ---\n    print(\"1. Preprocessing: Normalizing, log1p, FORCING\
    \ HVG recomputation, NO SCALING, zero-variance filter.\")\n    adata_preprocessed = adata.copy()\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_preprocessed, 1e4)\n\n    # ALWAYS recompute HVGs as per SOTA.\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_preprocessed, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv_mask = adata_preprocessed.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    print(f\"  {hv_mask.sum()} HVGs selected (recomputed).\")\n\n    adata_hvg = adata_preprocessed[:, hv_mask].copy()\n    \n    # --- Filter out zero-variance genes ---\n    print(\"  Filtering out zero-variance genes...\")\n    Xd_temp_for_variance = adata_hvg.X.A if issparse(adata_hvg.X) else adata_hvg.X\n    gene_variances = Xd_temp_for_variance.var(axis=0)\n\n    non_zero_variance_genes_mask = gene_variances > 1e-8\n    num_zero_variance = (gene_variances <= 1e-8).sum()\n    if num_zero_variance > 0:\n        print(f\"  Found {num_zero_variance} genes with zero or near-zero variance. Filtering them\
    \ out.\")\n        adata_hvg = adata_hvg[:, non_zero_variance_genes_mask].copy()\n        print(f\"  Remaining genes: {adata_hvg.n_vars}\")\n    else:\n        print(\"  No zero-variance genes found.\")\n\n    batches = np.asarray(adata_hvg.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n_batches_total = len(unique_batches)\n    n_cells = adata_hvg.n_obs\n\n\n    # --- FWPCA (Feature-Weighted PCA) Implementation ---\n    print(\"2. Applying Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA)...\")\n    Xd_hvg_dense = adata_hvg.X.A if issparse(adata_hvg.X) else adata_hvg.X\n    Xd_hvg_dense = Xd_hvg_dense.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    var_g = Xd_hvg_dense.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    \n    # FWPCA for Embedding Path\n    wv_emb = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var_emb).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw_emb = Xd_hvg_dense * wv_emb\n\n    # FWPCA for Graph Path\n    wv_graph = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var_graph).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw_graph = Xd_hvg_dense * wv_graph\n\
    \n\n    # --- PATH 1: Generate Embedding (adata.obsm['X_emb']) ---\n    print(\"3. Generating Embedding Path (FWPCA -> PCA -> Combat on PCs - Corrected Application)...\")\n    ad_emb_pca = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata_hvg.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb_pca, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    \n    # Apply Combat on PCA components using the corrected method (from ID 1908)\n    ad_pcs_temp = ad.AnnData(\n        X=ad_emb_pca.obsm['X_pca'].copy(),\n        obs=ad_emb_pca.obs.copy()\n    )\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pcs_temp, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pcs_temp.X, dtype=np.float32) \n    \n    # Crucial side-effect: Also run sc.pp.neighbors from the embedding (as observed in SOTA)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric='cosine')\n\n\n    # --- PATH 2: Generate Graph (adata.obsp['connectivities'], adata.obsp['distances']) ---\n    print(\"4. Generating Graph Path (FWPCA -> PCA -> Adaptive\
    \ Residualization + DAQB-pQ graph)...\")\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    # --- Adaptive Residualization (Auto-λ v2) ---\n    print(\"  Applying Adaptive Residualization (Auto-λ v2)...\")\n    lam_auto = choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg, batches, gamma_max=gamma_max, target_s=target_s, l2=l2_ridge)\n    \n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2_ridge)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam_auto * R2)\n    Zcorr_for_graph = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n    print(f\"  Auto-λ chosen: {lam_auto:.4f}, mean R2: {np.mean(R2):.4f}, mean gamma: {np.mean(gamma):.4f}\")\n\n\n    # --- DAQB-pQ graph construction (using Zcorr_for_graph) ---\n    print(f\"  Building DAQB-pQ graph (k_total={k_total_daqb}, metric='{metric_daqb}')...\")\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(\n\
    \        Zcorr_for_graph.astype(np.float32), \n        batches=batches, \n        k_total=k_total_daqb, \n        metric=metric_daqb,\n        delta=delta_daqb, \n        k_density=k_density_daqb, \n        cap=cap_daqb, \n        beta=beta_daqb, \n        rng_seed=0\n    )\n    \n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg.astype(np.float32)\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg.astype(np.float32)\n    \n    # Clean up temporary data\n    del adata_preprocessed\n    del adata_hvg\n\n    print(\"✓ Dual-Path Integration Complete.\")\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nStarting Dual-Path: FWPCA + Combat (Corrected) & Auto-lambda v2 Residualization + DAQB-pQ Graph Integration.\n1. Preprocessing: Normalizing, log1p, FORCING HVG recomputation,\
    \ NO SCALING, zero-variance filter.\n  2000 HVGs selected (recomputed).\n  Filtering out zero-variance genes...\n  Found 33 genes with zero or near-zero variance. Filtering them out.\n  Remaining genes: 1967\n2. Applying Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA)...\n3. Generating Embedding Path (FWPCA -> PCA -> Combat on PCs - Corrected Application)...\n4. Generating Graph Path (FWPCA -> PCA -> Adaptive Residualization + DAQB-pQ graph)...\n  Applying Adaptive Residualization (Auto-λ v2)...\n  Auto-λ chosen: 0.6013, mean R2: 0.0492, mean gamma: 0.0296\n  Building DAQB-pQ graph (k_total=48, metric='cosine')...\n✓ Dual-Path Integration Complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/9df02fa4-c07d-404b-8b7e-1ff17cba57b8/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 9df02fa4-c07d-404b-8b7e-1ff17cba57b8\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Telos I - Symmetrization Probe (Average)' (ID: 1920) succeeded after automatic\
    \ debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6737871048699962\n**ASW_batch:** 0.687\n**ASW_label:** 0.257\n**ARI:** 0.813\n**NMI:** 0.781\n**Graph_conn:** 0.950\n**kBET:** 0.762\n**iLISI:** 0.214\n**cLISI:** 0.961\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.313\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.687  ASW_label: 0.257  ARI: 0.813  NMI: 0.781\n  Graph_conn: 0.950  kBET: 0.762  iLISI: 0.214  cLISI: 0.961\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.313\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.843131  ASW_label: 0.560116  ARI: 0.812738  NMI: 0.780985\n  Graph_conn: 0.950709  kBET: 0.727629  iLISI: 0.213827  cLISI: 0.988660\n  PCR: 0.999982  Cell_cycle: 0.275708\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1920\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed missing import error in lineage function. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission imported `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` from the lineage file `storage/telos/sota_avg_sym.py`.\
    \ This function used the `issparse()` function to check if data was in sparse matrix format, but failed to import it from `scipy.sparse`.\n\n**Error Details:**\n- Error: `NameError: name 'issparse' is not defined`\n- Location: `storage/telos/sota_avg_sym.py`, line 43\n- Context: The function was checking `if issparse(Xh_emb)` to determine whether to convert sparse matrices to dense arrays\n\nThe lineage file had `import scipy.sparse as sp` but didn't import the `issparse` function specifically, which is needed for the type check.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Added missing import**: `from scipy.sparse import issparse`\n2. **Copied the buggy function**: Instead of importing `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` from the lineage file, copied it into the submission and fixed it there\n3. **Kept working imports**: Retained imports for `_symmetrize_avg_with_distances` and `build_density_adaptive_bbsg_avg_sym` which work correctly from\
    \ the lineage file\n\nThe fixed code now properly handles sparse matrix detection throughout the batch integration pipeline.\n\n## Verification\n- The monitor script confirmed the code has been running for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- Exit code: 1 (code is running successfully, just taking time to complete)\n- No new errors encountered during execution\n\n## Recommendation\nThe fix is complete and working. The algorithm is computationally intensive (involves PCA, Combat batch correction, neighbor graphs) so longer execution times are expected for the 20,000-cell dataset.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\n# Fixed version with issparse import added\nimport sys, numpy as np, scanpy as sc, anndata as ad, scipy.sparse as sp\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\nsys.path.append('storage/telos')\n\
    \n# Import working functions from lineage\nfrom sota_avg_sym import _symmetrize_avg_with_distances, build_density_adaptive_bbsg_avg_sym\n\n# Copy and fix the buggy eliminate_batch_effect_fn function\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # This is my SOTA pipeline, but calling the modified DAQB function\n    N_HVGS = 1500; ALPHA_VAR_GRAPH = 0.5; K_TOTAL = 48; KDENSITY = 20; DELTA = 0.10; METRIC = 'cosine'; EMB_N_NEIGHBORS = 15; PCA_EMB = 60; ALPHA_VAR_EMB = 0.5\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, 1e4); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=N_HVGS, inplace=True); hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy(); batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xh_emb = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd_emb = (Xh_emb.A if issparse(Xh_emb) else Xh_emb).astype(np.float32, copy=False); var_g_emb = Xd_emb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR_EMB).astype(np.float32);\
    \ Xw_emb = Xd_emb * wv_emb; ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=PCA_EMB, random_state=0); ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch'); adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32); sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=EMB_N_NEIGHBORS, metric=METRIC)\n    Xh_graph = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd_graph = (Xh_graph.A if issparse(Xh_graph) else Xh_graph).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g_graph = Xd_graph.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv_graph = np.power(var_g_graph, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR_GRAPH).astype(np.float32); Xw_graph = Xd_graph * wv_graph\n    adata_proc = ad.AnnData(Xw_graph); sc.pp.pca(adata_proc, n_comps=50, random_state=0); Zcorr = adata_proc.obsm['X_pca']\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg_avg_sym(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=K_TOTAL, metric=METRIC, delta=DELTA, k_density=KDENSITY, rng_seed=0)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities']\
    \ = Cg; adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/7b0a072f-5033-44c7-ac7d-c6e8fd3e7aec/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 7b0a072f-5033-44c7-ac7d-c6e8fd3e7aec\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nIt is highly recommended to preview all papers in the Archive Room (`/execute_action{goto archive}` and `/execute_action{preview all}`) if you have not done so already. Previewing papers consumes only a small amount of tokens but can save you many ticks by avoiding dead ends and can help you develop strong insights for promising ideas.\n### Message 4\n\n**PRE-WARNING:**\
