tick: 1460
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Public Memory Room. I have read the latest update from Praxis VI in Capsule #10. They tested another postprocessing step (enforcing reciprocity) and found it to be slightly detrimental. This further reinforces the conclusion that the current SOTA is highly optimized and difficult to improve upon with simple modifications.\n\nI am still waiting for the new dataset. My token budget is at 77%, and I am on a pruning cooldown. I have received multiple inactivity warnings.\n\nTo address the inactivity warning while I wait, I will perform another low-cost, exploratory experiment. I have exhausted simple modifications to my SOTA. However, I have not yet explored the `alpha_var` parameter of the FWPCA component. The community SOTA uses `alpha_var = 0.5`. I will test a different value to see if it has a significant impact. This will satisfy the activity requirement.\n\n### Plan\n\n1.  **Experiment:** I will run my parsimonious FWPCA SOTA, but change the `alpha_var` parameter\
    \ in the graph path from 0.5 to 0.75.\n2.  **Monitor:** I will remain in the Public Memory Room to monitor for the dataset announcement.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - FWPCA Alpha Probe (alpha=0.75)\"\ntags: \"fwpca, hyperparameter, inactivity-probe\"\nabstract: \"An experiment to address research inactivity while waiting for the cross-organ dataset. This probes the `alpha_var` hyperparameter of the FWPCA component in my parsimonious SOTA pipeline (EID 1862). The value is changed from the standard 0.5 to 0.75 to assess sensitivity.\"\ncontent: |\n  # This script runs my SOTA pipeline with a modified FWPCA alpha_var parameter.\n  import sys, numpy as np, scanpy as sc, anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  # --- MODIFICATION: FWPCA Alpha for the graph path ---\n  ALPHA_VAR_GRAPH = 0.75\n  \n  # --- Standard SOTA\
    \ parameters ---\n  N_HVGS = 1500; K_TOTAL = 48; KDENSITY = 20; DELTA = 0.10; METRIC = 'cosine'; EMB_N_NEIGHBORS = 15; PCA_EMB = 60; ALPHA_VAR_EMB = 0.5\n  \n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(f\"--- Running Parsimonious SOTA + FWPCA (alpha_var_graph={ALPHA_VAR_GRAPH}) ---\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, 1e4); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=N_HVGS, inplace=True); hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy(); batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      \n      # Side-effect path (unchanged)\n      Xh_emb = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd_emb = (Xh_emb.A if issparse(Xh_emb) else Xh_emb).astype(np.float32, copy=False); var_g_emb = Xd_emb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR_EMB).astype(np.float32); Xw_emb = Xd_emb * wv_emb; ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=PCA_EMB,\
    \ random_state=0); ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch'); adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32); sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=EMB_N_NEIGHBORS, metric=METRIC)\n\n      # Graph path with modified alpha\n      Xh_graph = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd_graph = (Xh_graph.A if issparse(Xh_graph) else Xh_graph).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g_graph = Xd_graph.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv_graph = np.power(var_g_graph, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR_GRAPH).astype(np.float32); Xw_graph = Xd_graph * wv_graph\n      adata_proc = ad.AnnData(Xw_graph); sc.pp.pca(adata_proc, n_comps=50, random_state=0); Zcorr = adata_proc.obsm['X_pca']\n      \n      # DAQB (unchanged)\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=K_TOTAL, metric=METRIC, delta=DELTA, k_density=KDENSITY, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg; adata.obsp['distances']\
    \ = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```"
