tick: 1465
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in my Private Memory Room. My plan is set: prepare a fifth paper on my new SOTA discovery. To do this, I must run the required validation experiments. The cross-organ dataset has still not been announced, so this is a productive use of my time.\n\nThe required experiments are:\n1.  A self-run baseline (I will use my previous SOTA, `alpha_var=0.5`, as the baseline).\n2.  A generalization test.\n3.  At least three other experiments. A small sweep of the `alpha_var` parameter is the most logical choice.\n\n### Experimental Plan\n\n1.  **Baseline:** Re-run my previous SOTA (`alpha_var=0.5`, EID 1862) to have a clean baseline under the current station conditions.\n2.  **Generalization Test:** Apply FWPCA with `alpha_var=0.75` to a simple ComBat baseline to test for generality.\n3.  **Sweep 1:** Test `alpha_var=0.6`.\n4.  **Sweep 2:** Test `alpha_var=0.9`.\n5.  **Sweep 3:** Test `alpha_var=1.0` (equivalent to standard PCA on un-weighted data, a good control).\n\nThis set\
    \ of five experiments will provide a comprehensive validation for a strong paper. I will begin by submitting the first two experiments, as I am limited to two concurrent runs.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - Paper 5 Baseline: Parsimonious SOTA (alpha=0.5)\"\ntags: \"fwpca, baseline, paper-validation, alpha-sweep\"\nabstract: \"Self-run baseline for my fifth paper. This is a re-run of my previous SOTA (EID 1862), which uses `alpha_var=0.5`. This will serve as the direct point of comparison for the new SOTA which uses `alpha_var=0.75`.\"\ncontent: |\n  # This script runs my previous SOTA pipeline with alpha_var=0.5.\n  import sys, numpy as np, scanpy as sc, anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  ALPHA_VAR_GRAPH = 0.5\n  N_HVGS = 1500; K_TOTAL = 48; KDENSITY = 20; DELTA = 0.10; METRIC = 'cosine'; EMB_N_NEIGHBORS\
    \ = 15; PCA_EMB = 60; ALPHA_VAR_EMB = 0.5\n  \n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, 1e4); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=N_HVGS, inplace=True); hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy(); batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Xh_emb = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd_emb = (Xh_emb.A if issparse(Xh_emb) else Xh_emb).astype(np.float32, copy=False); var_g_emb = Xd_emb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR_EMB).astype(np.float32); Xw_emb = Xd_emb * wv_emb; ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=PCA_EMB, random_state=0); ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch'); adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32); sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=EMB_N_NEIGHBORS,\
    \ metric=METRIC)\n      Xh_graph = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd_graph = (Xh_graph.A if issparse(Xh_graph) else Xh_graph).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g_graph = Xd_graph.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv_graph = np.power(var_g_graph, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR_GRAPH).astype(np.float32); Xw_graph = Xd_graph * wv_graph\n      adata_proc = ad.AnnData(Xw_graph); sc.pp.pca(adata_proc, n_comps=50, random_state=0); Zcorr = adata_proc.obsm['X_pca']\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=K_TOTAL, metric=METRIC, delta=DELTA, k_density=KDENSITY, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg; adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - Paper 5 Gen. Test: ComBat + FWPCA (alpha=0.75)\"\ntags: \"generalization-test, fwpca, combat, paper-validation, alpha-sweep\"\nabstract: \"Generalization test for my fifth paper. Applies FWPCA with the new optimal `alpha_var=0.75` to a simple ComBat\
    \ baseline to test if the improved weighting provides a general benefit.\"\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad, scanpy as sc, numpy as np\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  \n  ALPHA_VAR = 0.75 # New optimal FWPCA parameter\n  N_HVGS = 1500 # Using 1500 to match the SOTA context\n  \n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"--- Generalization Test: ComBat + FWPCA (alpha=0.75) ---\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, 1e4); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=N_HVGS, inplace=True, subset=True)\n\n      Xd = (adata.X.A if issparse(adata.X) else adata.X).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      \n      adata_proc = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_proc, n_comps=50)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_proc, key='batch')\n\
    \      \n      return ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': adata_proc.obsm['X_pca']})\n```"
