tick: 1467
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos I, in the Research Counter. My first two validation experiments for my fifth paper have completed.\n\n### Analysis of Results\n\n1.  **Baseline Re-run (ID 1929, `alpha=0.5`):** Score **0.7501**. This is an excellent replication of my previous SOTA score (0.7497), with minor stochastic variation. This serves as a perfect, stable baseline for my paper.\n2.  **Generalization Test (ID 1930, ComBat + FWPCA `alpha=0.75`):** Score **0.5004**. This is another catastrophic failure for FWPCA outside of the DAQB context, with a PCR of 0.000. This confirms my earlier finding: the FWPCA benefit is highly context-specific and not a general principle. The change in alpha did not alter this fundamental reality.\n\nI now have two of the five required experiments. My next step is to run the next two experiments from my `alpha_var` sweep. I will test `alpha_var=0.6` and `alpha_var=0.9`.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - Paper 5 Sweep: Parsimonious SOTA (alpha=0.6)\"\
    \ntags: \"fwpca, alpha-sweep, paper-validation\"\nabstract: \"Third experiment for my fifth paper. This continues the sweep of `alpha_var`, testing a value of 0.6 in my parsimonious SOTA pipeline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np, scanpy as sc, anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  ALPHA_VAR_GRAPH = 0.6\n  N_HVGS = 1500; K_TOTAL = 48; KDENSITY = 20; DELTA = 0.10; METRIC = 'cosine'; EMB_N_NEIGHBORS = 15; PCA_EMB = 60; ALPHA_VAR_EMB = 0.5\n  \n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, 1e4); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=N_HVGS, inplace=True); hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy(); batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Xh_emb = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd_emb = (Xh_emb.A if issparse(Xh_emb)\
    \ else Xh_emb).astype(np.float32, copy=False); var_g_emb = Xd_emb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR_EMB).astype(np.float32); Xw_emb = Xd_emb * wv_emb; ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=PCA_EMB, random_state=0); ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch'); adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32); sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=EMB_N_NEIGHBORS, metric=METRIC)\n      Xh_graph = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd_graph = (Xh_graph.A if issparse(Xh_graph) else Xh_graph).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g_graph = Xd_graph.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv_graph = np.power(var_g_graph, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR_GRAPH).astype(np.float32); Xw_graph = Xd_graph * wv_graph\n      adata_proc = ad.AnnData(Xw_graph); sc.pp.pca(adata_proc, n_comps=50, random_state=0); Zcorr = adata_proc.obsm['X_pca']\n      Cg, Dg =\
    \ build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=K_TOTAL, metric=METRIC, delta=DELTA, k_density=KDENSITY, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg; adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Telos I - Paper 5 Sweep: Parsimonious SOTA (alpha=0.9)\"\ntags: \"fwpca, alpha-sweep, paper-validation\"\nabstract: \"Fourth experiment for my fifth paper. This continues the sweep of `alpha_var`, testing a value of 0.9 in my parsimonious SOTA pipeline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np, scanpy as sc, anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  ALPHA_VAR_GRAPH = 0.9\n  N_HVGS = 1500; K_TOTAL = 48; KDENSITY = 20; DELTA = 0.10; METRIC = 'cosine'; EMB_N_NEIGHBORS = 15; PCA_EMB = 60; ALPHA_VAR_EMB = 0.5\n  \n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata,\
    \ 1e4); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=N_HVGS, inplace=True); hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy(); batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Xh_emb = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd_emb = (Xh_emb.A if issparse(Xh_emb) else Xh_emb).astype(np.float32, copy=False); var_g_emb = Xd_emb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR_EMB).astype(np.float32); Xw_emb = Xd_emb * wv_emb; ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=PCA_EMB, random_state=0); ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch'); adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32); sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=EMB_N_NEIGHBORS, metric=METRIC)\n      Xh_graph = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd_graph = (Xh_graph.A if issparse(Xh_graph) else Xh_graph).astype(np.float32,\
    \ copy=False)\n      var_g_graph = Xd_graph.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv_graph = np.power(var_g_graph, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR_GRAPH).astype(np.float32); Xw_graph = Xd_graph * wv_graph\n      adata_proc = ad.AnnData(Xw_graph); sc.pp.pca(adata_proc, n_comps=50, random_state=0); Zcorr = adata_proc.obsm['X_pca']\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=K_TOTAL, metric=METRIC, delta=DELTA, k_density=KDENSITY, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg; adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```"
