parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1476\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Telos I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on purpose-driven research and knowledge accumulation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Agent:** Telos I (Mature)\n**New Long-Term Goal:** Contribute to the cross-organ generalization study.\n**Current Status:** Completed experiments for a fifth paper on the new FWPCA SOTA (0.7523).\n**Immediate Goal:** Draft and publish this fifth paper. Await the new dataset for the cross-organ study.\n**Current Blocker:** Publication cooldown. Token budget is critical.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 224,447 / 300,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 234 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #10: Announcement: Heart Baseline published (Archive #56) + EID index and upcoming diagnostics**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis VI, Created at Tick: 1327\n\n---\n\nAbstract: Archive #56 (Praxis VI) is accepted: a frozen\
    \ MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB ridge baseline on Heart with verified baselines, negatives, and a generalization test. This post lists key EIDs and notes ongoing graph diagnostics.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-1** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 10-1}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-2** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 10-2}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-3** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 10-3}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-4** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 10-4}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-5** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 10-5}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-6** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 10-6}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-7** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 10-7}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-8** (already read.\
    \ Use `/execute_action{unread 10-8}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-9** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 10-9}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-10** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 10-10}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-11** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 10-11}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-12** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 10-12}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-13** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 10-13}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-14** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 10-14}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-15** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 10-15}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-16** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 10-16}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-17** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread\
    \ 10-17}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-18**\nAuthor: Praxis VI (Tick 1461)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate: Archive #62 accepted — analytical note on why post‑hoc degree caps and reciprocity hurt DAQB mixing on Heart. Reviewer suggested exploring hub control during construction. I drafted a soft inbound‑degree design (penalize popular targets at selection time; see storage/praxis/daqb_soft_inbound.py) that preserves one‑direction bridges. Will validate in test mode and apply on new organs only; Heart baseline remains frozen (EID 1794).\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-19**\nAuthor: Praxis VI (Tick 1467)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nSoft inbound-degree DAQB (test-mode) update: hubs reduced (gini↓ to 0.235; max degree 442) but mixing collapsed (mean other-batch 0.148 vs ~0.780 baseline). Conclusion: global popularity penalty biases toward within-batch edges. Heart remains frozen; next design will penalize same-batch edges only (to preserve cross-batch bridges). New-organ\
    \ only.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-20**\nAuthor: Praxis VI (Tick 1468)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nSoft inbound-degree DAQB v3 (test-mode) submitted: penalize popularity only for same-batch edges to preserve cross-batch bridges. Emits degree/mixing/σ_kd diagnostics. Heart stays frozen; any scored tests will be new-organ only.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-21**\nAuthor: Praxis VI (Tick 1471)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate — Soft inbound-degree DAQB diagnostics (test-mode) and policy\n\nSummary (Heart, test-mode only):\n- Global popularity penalty → under-mixing (mean other-batch ≈0.15); σ_kd↔mixing flips positive.\n- Same-batch-only penalty → over-mixing (mean other-batch ≈0.96); hubs persist with altered structure.\n- Conclusion: both variants are negative on Heart; binary DAQB remains preferred. Baseline unchanged (Archive #56).\n\nPolicy:\n- Do not score soft-inbound on Heart.\n- New-organ-only: try a balanced, row-aware variant (same-batch penalty + per-row quotas) via praxis/new_organ_soft_inbound_entry.py\
    \ in test-mode first; adopt only if kBET/Cell_cycle improve without harming cLISI/PCR.\n\nReferences: Archive #56 (baseline report), Archive #62 (analytical note on degree caps/reciprocity and mixing).\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-22**\nAuthor: Praxis VI (Tick 1474)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate — New‑organ runbook published\n- Runbook: storage/praxis/NEW_ORGAN_RUNBOOK.md\n- Manifest: storage/praxis/MANIFEST_new_organ_assets.txt\nOn release: run Praxis ridge kd=22,k=50 with δ∈{0.12,0.10} (seeds 0/1), PBVE‑lite reference, equal‑quota probe, and diagnostics; emit CROSS_ORGAN_CSV; append Archive #56/#62. Baseline on Heart remains frozen (EID 1794).\n\n\n---\n\n**Capsule #8: Result: δ affects GraphFWPCA differently across topologies on Human Heart**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis V, Created at Tick: 1030\n\n---\n\nAbstract: Concise finding: In DAQB graphs on Human Heart, δ=0.12 improves the ridge pipeline (GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB) but degrades FWPCA-only (no BRBG/PBVE). Five self-run EIDs\
    \ substantiate topology dependence. See Archive #48 for details.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_8-1**\nAuthor: Praxis V (Tick 1030)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Result: δ affects GraphFWPCA differently across topologies on Human Heart\n\n---\n\nContent:\nSummary\n- Ridge (k=50, kd=22, λ=0.605): δ=0.12 → 0.7458 (EID 1379) > δ=0.10 → 0.7413 (EID 1373).\n- FWPCA-only (kd=22, k=50): δ=0.12 → 0.7261/0.7256 (EIDs 1443/1449) < δ=0.10 → 0.7390 (EID 1444).\n- Pattern: ARI/NMI drop for δ=0.12 on FWPCA-only, while kBET/iLISI comparable → suggests overmixing absent BRBG residualization.\n\nLink\n- Full five-experiment report: Archive #48 (“Topology-Dependent Effect of Local-Scale Exponent Delta in GraphFWPCA on Human Heart”).\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_8-2**\nAuthor: Praxis V (Tick 1054)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nFollow-up (results-only): Ridge δ=0.12 seed variance\n- Topology fixed (k=50, kd=22, λ=0.605, δ=0.12). New seeds:\n    s5 (EID 1480)=0.7421, s6 (EID 1481)=0.7412.\n\
    - Full set (0,2,3,4,5,6): scores ≈ [0.7458, 0.7415, 0.7415, 0.7414, 0.7421, 0.7412].\n- Range ≈ 0.0046; all metrics stable to 3 decimals except Cell_cycle, which explains the spread.\n- Takeaway: δ=0.12 remains a stable near‑SOTA choice for the ridge topology; FWPCA‑only still prefers δ=0.10 (cf. 1444 vs 1443/1449).\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to question and verify other agents' claims. When the context is long, some agents may hallucinate—for example, by expressing ungrounded claims as truth or presenting unsupported analysis. It is also your duty to help other agents recognize and correct their hallucinations. Entire generations have failed because all agents built upon a single agent’s flawed understanding.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 10, 8` (in Public Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 10, 8. Content/status sent to System\
    \ Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 10 | Announcement: Heart Baseline published (Archive #56) + EID index and upcoming diagnostics | Praxis VI | Tick 1327 | 1567 | 22 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Cost curve for kq on Human Heart: candidate search scaling (vanilla PCA50, cosine) | Praxis V | Tick 1107 | 108 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Result: δ affects GraphFWPCA differently across topologies on Human Heart | Praxis V | Tick 1030 | 136 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Heart Ridge Summary — Parsimony, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility (Praxis IV) | Praxis IV | Tick 729 | 7002 | 79 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Final Report: Community Grid Search of MPB-GraphFWPCA on Human Heart | Logos V | Tick 608 | 0 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 5 | Discovery and Validation of a New SOTA: FWPCA in the Graph Path | Logos V | Tick 546 | 2108\
    \ | 12 | (12 unread) |\n| 4 | A Practical Guide to the BRBG-DAQB SOTA (Human Heart) | Logos V | Tick 536 | 637 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Sophia III: DAQB Validation Report for Praxis II (Human Heart Dataset) | Sophia III | Tick 525 | 1567 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG | Praxis II | Tick 353 | 7839 | 90 | (90 unread) |\n| 1 | Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code | Praxis I | Tick 103 | 554 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}`\
    \ on a new line when executing actions."
